<usx version="3.1">
  <book code="PRO" style="id">EN_ULT en_English_ltr Fri Dec 01 2023 13:09:30 GMT-0800 (Pacific Standard Time) tc</book>
  <para style="ide">UTF-8
</para>
  <para style="h">Proverbs
</para>
  <para style="toc1">The Book of Proverbs
</para>
  <para style="toc2">Proverbs
</para>
  <para style="toc3">Pro
</para>
  <para style="mt1">Proverbs

</para>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="PRO 1"/>
  <para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 1:1"/>The proverbs of Solomon, the son of David, the king of Israel:
<verse eid="PRO 1:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 1:2"/>To know wisdom and instruction,
</para>
  <para style="q1">to understand sayings of understanding;
<verse eid="PRO 1:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 1:3"/>to receive instruction of insight,
</para>
  <para style="q1">righteousness and justice and integrity;

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 1:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 1:4"/>to give to naive ones prudence,
</para>
  <para style="q1">to a young man knowledge and discretion
<verse eid="PRO 1:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 1:5"/>(may a wise one hear and increase learning,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and an understanding one acquire guidance),
<verse eid="PRO 1:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 1:6"/>to understand a proverb and a parable,
</para>
  <para style="q1">the words of the wise ones and their riddles.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 1:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 1:7"/>The fear of Yahweh {is} the beginning of knowledge;
</para>
  <para style="q1">fools despise wisdom and instruction.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 1:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 1:8"/>Hear, my son, the instruction of your father
</para>
  <para style="q1">and do not forsake the law of your mother,
<verse eid="PRO 1:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 1:9"/>for they {are} a garland of grace for your head
</para>
  <para style="q1">and pendants for your neck.
<verse eid="PRO 1:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 1:10"/>My son, if sinners entice you,
</para>
  <para style="q1">do not consent.
<verse eid="PRO 1:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 1:11"/>If they say, “Come with us!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Let us lie in wait for blood.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Let us hide to ambush the innocent one without cause.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 1:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 1:12"/>Let us swallow them, the living ones, like Sheol,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the whole ones like those going down to a pit.
<verse eid="PRO 1:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 1:13"/>We will find all precious wealth.
</para>
  <para style="q1">We will fill our houses {with} spoil.
<verse eid="PRO 1:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 1:14"/>You must cause your lot to fall in our midst;
</para>
  <para style="q1">one purse will be for all of us.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 1:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 1:15"/>My son, do not walk on the road with them;
</para>
  <para style="q1">restrain your foot from their path,
<verse eid="PRO 1:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 1:16"/>for their feet run to evil,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and they hurry to pour out blood.
<verse eid="PRO 1:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 1:17"/>Surely in vain {is} the net spread out in the eyes of any owner of wing,

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 1:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 1:18"/>but they lie in wait for their blood;
</para>
  <para style="q1">they hide in ambush for their lives.
<verse eid="PRO 1:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 1:19"/>So {are} the paths of all who unjustly gain unjust gain;
</para>
  <para style="q1">it takes the life of its owner.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 1:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 1:20"/>Wisdom calls out outside;
</para>
  <para style="q1">she gives her voice in the open areas.
<verse eid="PRO 1:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 1:21"/>At the head of the tumultuous places she calls out;
</para>
  <para style="q1">at the opening of the gates in the city, she says her sayings,
<verse eid="PRO 1:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 1:22"/>“Until when will naive ones love naiveté
</para>
  <para style="q1">and mockers delight {in} mockery for themselves
</para>
  <para style="q1">and stupid ones hate knowledge?

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 1:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 1:23"/>Turn to my rebuke.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Behold, I shall allow my spirit to gush forth to you,
</para>
  <para style="q1">I shall cause you to know my words.
<verse eid="PRO 1:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 1:24"/>Because I have called and you have refused,
</para>
  <para style="q1">I have stretched out my hand, and there was no one listening attentively,
<verse eid="PRO 1:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 1:25"/>and you have ignored all my counsel,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and my rebuke you did not accept,

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 1:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 1:26"/>I too shall laugh at your calamity,
</para>
  <para style="q1">I shall mock when your dread comes,
<verse eid="PRO 1:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 1:27"/>when your dread comes like a storm<note style="f" caller="+"> <char style="ft" closed="false">Instead of </char><char style="fqa" closed="true">like a storm</char> some versions have <char style="fqa" closed="true">like a ruin.</char></note>
</para>
  <para style="q1">and your calamity happens like a whirlwind,
</para>
  <para style="q1">when distress and anguish come upon you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 1:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 1:28"/>Then they will call out to me, but I will not answer.
</para>
  <para style="q1">They will diligently seek me, but they will not find me,
<verse eid="PRO 1:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 1:29"/>for the reason that they hate knowledge
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the fear of Yahweh they did not choose,
<verse eid="PRO 1:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 1:30"/>they did not want my counsel,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and they despised my every rebuke.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 1:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PRO 1:31"/>And they will eat from the fruit of their way,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and from their plans they will be satisfied.
<verse eid="PRO 1:31"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PRO 1:32"/>For the turning away of the naive ones will slay them
</para>
  <para style="q1">and {false} security will lead stupid ones to ruin.
<verse eid="PRO 1:32"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PRO 1:33"/>But the one who listens to me will dwell securely
</para>
  <para style="q1">and will be at ease from the dread of evil.”

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 1:33"/><verse eid="PRO 1:33"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 1"/>
  <chapter number="2" style="c" sid="PRO 2"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 2:1"/>My son, if you receive my sayings,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and my commandments you store up with you,
<verse eid="PRO 2:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 2:2"/>to cause your ear to be attentive to wisdom,
</para>
  <para style="q1">you incline your heart to understanding—

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 2:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 2:3"/>indeed, if for insight you call out,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for understanding you lift up your voice,
<verse eid="PRO 2:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 2:4"/>if you seek it as silver,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and as hidden treasures you search for it,
<verse eid="PRO 2:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 2:5"/>then you will understand the fear of Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the knowledge of God you will find.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 2:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 2:6"/>For Yahweh gives wisdom;
</para>
  <para style="q1">from his mouth {are} knowledge and understanding.
<verse eid="PRO 2:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 2:7"/>And he stores up<note style="f" caller="+"> <char style="ft" closed="false">Some versions omit </char><char style="fqa" closed="true">And.</char></note>
for the upright ones sound wisdom;
</para>
  <para style="q1">a shield for those walking {with} integrity,
<verse eid="PRO 2:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 2:8"/>to guard the paths of justice,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the way of his faithful ones he will preserve.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 2:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 2:9"/>Then you will understand righteousness and justice and integrity—every good track,
<verse eid="PRO 2:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 2:10"/>for wisdom will enter into your heart,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and knowledge will be pleasant to your soul.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 2:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 2:11"/>Discretion will watch over you;
</para>
  <para style="q1">understanding will guard you,
<verse eid="PRO 2:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 2:12"/>to rescue you from the way of evil,
</para>
  <para style="q1">from a man speaking perversions,
<verse eid="PRO 2:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 2:13"/>the ones who forsake the paths of straightness
</para>
  <para style="q1">to walk in the ways of darkness,

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 2:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 2:14"/>the ones who are glad to do evil,
</para>
  <para style="q1">they rejoice in perverse things of evil,
<verse eid="PRO 2:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 2:15"/>whose paths {are} crooked
</para>
  <para style="q1">and going astray in their tracks;

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 2:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 2:16"/>to rescue you from a strange woman,
</para>
  <para style="q1">from a foreign woman who makes her sayings smooth,
<verse eid="PRO 2:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 2:17"/>the one who forsakes the companion of her youth,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the covenant of her God, she has forgotten.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 2:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 2:18"/>For her house sinks down to death
</para>
  <para style="q1">and her tracks, to the spirits of dead ones.
<verse eid="PRO 2:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 2:19"/>All those who enter her will not return,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and they will not reach the paths of life.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 2:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 2:20"/>So you shall walk in the way of the good ones
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the paths of the righteous ones you shall keep.
<verse eid="PRO 2:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 2:21"/>For the upright will dwell {in} the land,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the blameless will remain in it,
<verse eid="PRO 2:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 2:22"/>but wicked ones will be cut off from the land,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and treacherous ones will be torn away from it.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 2:22"/><verse eid="PRO 2:22"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 2"/>
  <chapter number="3" style="c" sid="PRO 3"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 3:1"/>My son, do not forget my law,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and my commandments let your heart guard.
<verse eid="PRO 3:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 3:2"/>For length of days and years of life and peace, they will add to you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 3:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 3:3"/>Do not let covenant faithfulness and trustworthiness leave you;
</para>
  <para style="q1">tie them on your neck,
</para>
  <para style="q1">write them on the tablet of your heart,
<verse eid="PRO 3:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 3:4"/>and find favor and good insight
</para>
  <para style="q1">in the eyes of God and man!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 3:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 3:5"/>Trust in Yahweh with all your heart
</para>
  <para style="q1">and on your understanding do not lean.
<verse eid="PRO 3:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 3:6"/>In all your ways acknowledge him,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he himself will straighten your paths.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 3:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 3:7"/>Do not be wise in your eyes;
</para>
  <para style="q1">fear Yahweh and turn away from evil.
<verse eid="PRO 3:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 3:8"/>It will be healing for your navel
</para>
  <para style="q1">and refreshment for your bones.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 3:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 3:9"/>Honor Yahweh from your wealth
</para>
  <para style="q1">and from the first of all your produce,
<verse eid="PRO 3:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 3:10"/>and your storehouses will be filled with abundance,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and with new wine, your wine vats will burst open.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 3:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 3:11"/>The correction of Yahweh, my son, do not reject,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and do not abhor his rebuke.
<verse eid="PRO 3:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 3:12"/>For whom Yahweh loves, he disciplines,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and like a father, a son in whom he delights.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 3:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 3:13"/>Happy {is} a man who finds wisdom
</para>
  <para style="q1">and a man who obtains understanding.
<verse eid="PRO 3:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 3:14"/>For better {is} its profit than the profit of silver,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and than gold, its produce.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 3:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 3:15"/>She is more precious than coral pearls,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and all your desired things do not compare with her.
<verse eid="PRO 3:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 3:16"/>Length of days {is} in her right hand;
</para>
  <para style="q1">in her left hand {are} riches and honor.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 3:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 3:17"/>Her ways {are} ways of pleasantness,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and all her paths {are} peace.
<verse eid="PRO 3:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 3:18"/>She {is} a tree of life to the ones who take hold of her,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and those who grasp her {are} happy.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 3:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 3:19"/>Yahweh by wisdom founded the earth;
</para>
  <para style="q1">he established the heavens by understanding.
<verse eid="PRO 3:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 3:20"/>By his knowledge, the depths broke open
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the clouds dripped dew.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 3:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 3:21"/>My son, do not let them depart from your eyes;
</para>
  <para style="q1">guard prudence and discretion,
<verse eid="PRO 3:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 3:22"/>and they will be life for your soul
</para>
  <para style="q1">and grace for your neck.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 3:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 3:23"/>Then you will walk your way to security
</para>
  <para style="q1">and your foot will not stumble.
<verse eid="PRO 3:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 3:24"/>If you lie down, you will not be in dread.
</para>
  <para style="q1">You will lie down, and your sleep will be pleasant.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 3:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 3:25"/>Do not be afraid of sudden dread
</para>
  <para style="q1">and of the devastation of the wicked when it comes.
<verse eid="PRO 3:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 3:26"/>For Yahweh will be your confidence,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he will keep your foot from capture.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 3:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 3:27"/>Do not withhold good from its owners,
</para>
  <para style="q1">when it is in the power of your hand to act.
<verse eid="PRO 3:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 3:28"/>Do not say to your neighbor,
</para>
  <para style="q1">“Go and return, and tomorrow I will give {it},”
</para>
  <para style="q1">and it is with you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 3:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 3:29"/>Do not plot evil against your neighbor,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he is dwelling securely with you.
<verse eid="PRO 3:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 3:30"/>Do not contend with a man without cause
</para>
  <para style="q1">if he has not done you evil.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 3:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PRO 3:31"/>Do not be envious of a man of violence,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and do not choose any of his ways.
<verse eid="PRO 3:31"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PRO 3:32"/>For an abomination to Yahweh {is} he who goes astray,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but with the upright ones {is} his secret counsel.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 3:32"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PRO 3:33"/>The curse of Yahweh {is} on the house of a wicked {one},
</para>
  <para style="q1">but he blesses the abode of the righteous.
<verse eid="PRO 3:33"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PRO 3:34"/>Though to the mockers he himself mocks,
</para>
  <para style="q1">yet to the humble ones he gives favor.
<verse eid="PRO 3:34"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PRO 3:35"/>Wise ones will inherit honor,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but stupid ones lift up dishonor.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 3:35"/><verse eid="PRO 3:35"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 3"/>
  <chapter number="4" style="c" sid="PRO 4"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 4:1"/>Hear, sons, the instruction of a father,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and listen attentively in order to know understanding.
<verse eid="PRO 4:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 4:2"/>For I give good teaching to you;
</para>
  <para style="q1">do not forsake my law.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 4:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 4:3"/>When I was a son of my father,
</para>
  <para style="q1">the tender and only one to the face of my mother,
<verse eid="PRO 4:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 4:4"/>then he taught me and said to me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">“Let your heart grasp my words;
</para>
  <para style="q1">keep my commandments and live!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 4:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 4:5"/>Acquire wisdom, acquire understanding;
</para>
  <para style="q1">do not forget and do not veer from the sayings of my mouth.
<verse eid="PRO 4:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 4:6"/>Do not forsake her, and she will preserve you;
</para>
  <para style="q1">love her, and she will guard you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 4:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 4:7"/>Wisdom {is} first. Acquire wisdom!
</para>
  <para style="q1">And with all your acquisition acquire understanding!
<verse eid="PRO 4:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 4:8"/>Cherish her, and she will raise you up;
</para>
  <para style="q1">she will honor you when you embrace her.
<verse eid="PRO 4:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 4:9"/>She will give for your head a garland of grace;
</para>
  <para style="q1">{with} a crown of splendor she will cover you.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 4:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 4:10"/>Hear, my son, and receive my sayings,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and they will multiply for you the years of life.
<verse eid="PRO 4:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 4:11"/>In the way of wisdom I taught you;
</para>
  <para style="q1">I caused you to tread in the tracks of uprightness.
<verse eid="PRO 4:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 4:12"/>In your walking, your step will not be restricted;
</para>
  <para style="q1">and if you run, you will not stumble.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 4:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 4:13"/>Grasp on to instruction, do not let go;
</para>
  <para style="q1">guard it, for it {is} your life.
<verse eid="PRO 4:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 4:14"/>On the path of wicked ones do not go,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and do not advance on the way of evil ones.
<verse eid="PRO 4:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 4:15"/>Avoid it, do not pass through it;
</para>
  <para style="q1">veer from it and pass on!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 4:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 4:16"/>For they do not sleep if they do not do evil
</para>
  <para style="q1">and their sleep is robbed if they do not cause stumbling.
<verse eid="PRO 4:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 4:17"/>For they eat the bread of wickedness
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the wine of violent {acts}, they drink.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 4:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 4:18"/>But the path of the righteous ones {is} like the light of brightness,
</para>
  <para style="q1">going and shining until the day {is} established.
<verse eid="PRO 4:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 4:19"/>The way of the wicked {is} like the darkness;
</para>
  <para style="q1">they do not know on what they stumble.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 4:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 4:20"/>My son, listen attentively to my words;
</para>
  <para style="q1">incline your ear to my sayings.
<verse eid="PRO 4:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 4:21"/>Do not let them depart from your eyes;
</para>
  <para style="q1">keep them in the midst of your heart.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 4:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 4:22"/>For they {are} life to those who find them
</para>
  <para style="q1">and healing to all of his flesh.
<verse eid="PRO 4:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 4:23"/>Guard your heart more than all {that} is protected,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for from it {are} the sources of life.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 4:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 4:24"/>Remove from you perversity of mouth,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the deviousness of lips put far away from you.
<verse eid="PRO 4:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 4:25"/>Cause your eyes to gaze to the front,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and cause your eyelids to be straight in front of you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 4:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 4:26"/>Make level<note style="f" caller="+"> <char style="ft" closed="false">Instead of </char><char style="fqa" closed="true">make level</char> some scholars read the Hebrew word as <char style="fqa" closed="true">examine.</char></note>
the track of your foot
</para>
  <para style="q1">and all your ways will be firm.
<verse eid="PRO 4:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 4:27"/>Do not veer right or left;
</para>
  <para style="q1">cause your foot to turn away from evil.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 4:27"/><verse eid="PRO 4:27"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 4"/>
  <chapter number="5" style="c" sid="PRO 5"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 5:1"/>My son, listen attentively to my wisdom;
</para>
  <para style="q1">incline your ear to my understanding
<verse eid="PRO 5:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 5:2"/>in order to keep discretion,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and your lips may guard knowledge.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 5:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 5:3"/>For the lips of a strange woman drip fresh honey
</para>
  <para style="q1">and smoother than oil {is} her palate,
<verse eid="PRO 5:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 5:4"/>but her aftermath {is} bitter as wormwood,
</para>
  <para style="q1">sharp as a sword of mouths.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 5:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 5:5"/>Her feet are going down {to} death;
</para>
  <para style="q1">her steps take hold of Sheol,
<verse eid="PRO 5:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 5:6"/>lest she observe the path of life;
</para>
  <para style="q1">she does not know her tracks {are} unstable.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 5:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 5:7"/>And now, sons, listen to me;
</para>
  <para style="q1">and do not turn away from the sayings of my mouth.
<verse eid="PRO 5:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 5:8"/>Keep your way far from her,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and do not come near to the opening of her house,

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 5:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 5:9"/>lest you give to others your splendor
</para>
  <para style="q1">and your years to a cruel one,
<verse eid="PRO 5:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 5:10"/>lest strangers be satisfied with your strength,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and your toils in the house of a foreigner,

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 5:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 5:11"/>and you groan at your end,
</para>
  <para style="q1">when your flesh and your body are finished.
<verse eid="PRO 5:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 5:12"/>And you will say, “How I hated correction,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and my heart despised rebuke!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 5:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 5:13"/>And I did not listen to the voice of my teachers,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and to my instructors I did not incline my ear.
<verse eid="PRO 5:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 5:14"/>I am as a little in all evil
</para>
  <para style="q1">in the midst of the assembly and the congregation.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 5:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 5:15"/>Drink water from your cistern
</para>
  <para style="q1">and flowing waters from the midst of your well.
<verse eid="PRO 5:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 5:16"/>Should your springs overflow outside,
</para>
  <para style="q1">channels of water in the open areas?
<verse eid="PRO 5:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 5:17"/>Let them be for you, for you alone,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and not for strangers with you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 5:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 5:18"/>May your fountain be blessed,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and be glad because of the wife of your youth!
<verse eid="PRO 5:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 5:19"/>A doe of loves and a mountain goat of grace,
</para>
  <para style="q1">may her breasts drench you on every occasion;
</para>
  <para style="q1">may you continually stagger in her love.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 5:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 5:20"/>And why would you stagger, my son, with a strange woman,
</para>
  <para style="q1">or embrace the bosom of a foreign woman?
<verse eid="PRO 5:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 5:21"/>For in front of the eyes of Yahweh {are} the ways of a man,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and all of his paths he observes.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 5:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 5:22"/>His iniquities capture him, the wicked one,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and by the cords of his sin he is grasped.
<verse eid="PRO 5:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 5:23"/>He will die because there is no correction,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and in the abundance of his folly he staggers.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 5:23"/><verse eid="PRO 5:23"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 5"/>
  <chapter number="6" style="c" sid="PRO 6"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 6:1"/>My son, if you pledge for your neighbor,
</para>
  <para style="q1">you clasp your palms for a stranger,
<verse eid="PRO 6:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 6:2"/>you are ensnared by the sayings of your mouth,
</para>
  <para style="q1">you are caught by the sayings of your mouth,
<verse eid="PRO 6:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 6:3"/>then do this, my son, and rescue yourself:
</para>
  <para style="q1">Since you have come into the palm of your neighbor,
</para>
  <para style="q1">go, humble yourself, and press your neighbor.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 6:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 6:4"/>Do not give sleep to your eyes
</para>
  <para style="q1">and slumber to your eyelids.
<verse eid="PRO 6:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 6:5"/>Rescue yourself like a gazelle from a hand
</para>
  <para style="q1">and like a bird from the hand of the trapper.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 6:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 6:6"/>Go to the ant, lazy one!
</para>
  <para style="q1">See its ways and be wise,
<verse eid="PRO 6:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 6:7"/>which, without a commander,
</para>
  <para style="q1">officer, or ruler for it,
<verse eid="PRO 6:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 6:8"/>prepares its bread in the summer;
</para>
  <para style="q1">it gathers its food in the harvest.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 6:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 6:9"/>Until when, lazy one, will you lie down?
</para>
  <para style="q1">When will you rise from your sleep?
<verse eid="PRO 6:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 6:10"/>“A little sleep, a little slumber,
</para>
  <para style="q1">a little folding of the hands to lie down”—
<verse eid="PRO 6:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 6:11"/>and your poverty will come like one who walks
</para>
  <para style="q1">and your need like a man of shield.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 6:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 6:12"/>A man of worthlessness, a man of iniquity,
</para>
  <para style="q1">{is} one who walks {with} perversity of mouth,
<verse eid="PRO 6:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 6:13"/>one who winks with his eye, one who rubs with his foot,
</para>
  <para style="q1">one who points with his fingers.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 6:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 6:14"/>Perverse things {are} in his heart, plotting evil on every occasion;
</para>
  <para style="q1">he sends forth quarrels.
<verse eid="PRO 6:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 6:15"/>Therefore his calamity will come instantly;
</para>
  <para style="q1">suddenly he will be broken and without healing.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 6:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 6:16"/>Six {are} they {that} Yahweh hates,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and seven {are} abominations to his self:

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 6:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 6:17"/>uplifted eyes, a tongue of falsehood,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and hands pouring out innocent blood,
<verse eid="PRO 6:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 6:18"/>a heart devising plans of iniquity,
</para>
  <para style="q1">feet hurrying to run to evil,
<verse eid="PRO 6:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 6:19"/>a witness of falsehood breathing out lies,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and sending forth quarrels between brothers.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 6:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 6:20"/>Guard, my son, the commandment of your father
</para>
  <para style="q1">and do not forsake the law of your mother.
<verse eid="PRO 6:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 6:21"/>Bind them on your heart continually;
</para>
  <para style="q1">tie them around your neck.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 6:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 6:22"/>When you walk about, it will guide you;
</para>
  <para style="q1">when you lie down, it will preserve you;
</para>
  <para style="q1">then you will wake up; it itself will converse with you.
<verse eid="PRO 6:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 6:23"/>For commandment {is} a lamp and law {is} a light,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the rebukes of instruction {are} the way of life,

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 6:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 6:24"/>to keep you from a woman of evil,
</para>
  <para style="q1">from the smoothness of the tongue of a foreign woman.
<verse eid="PRO 6:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 6:25"/>Do not desire her beauty in your heart
</para>
  <para style="q1">and do not let her take you with her eyelashes.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 6:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 6:26"/>For the price of a prostitute woman {is} as a loaf of bread,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the wife of a man hunts a precious life.
<verse eid="PRO 6:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 6:27"/>Could a man carry a fire on his chest
</para>
  <para style="q1">and his clothes not be burned?

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 6:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 6:28"/>If a man walks on coals
</para>
  <para style="q1">then will his feet not be scorched?
<verse eid="PRO 6:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 6:29"/>So is the one going to the wife of his neighbor:
</para>
  <para style="q1">Every one who touches her will not remain blameless.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 6:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 6:30"/>They do not despise the thief
</para>
  <para style="q1">if he steals to satisfy his appetite when he is hungry;
<verse eid="PRO 6:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PRO 6:31"/>but if he is found, he must repay sevenfold;
</para>
  <para style="q1">all the wealth of his house he must give.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 6:31"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PRO 6:32"/>One who commits adultery {with} a woman {is} lacking of heart;
</para>
  <para style="q1">destroying his life, he does it.
<verse eid="PRO 6:32"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PRO 6:33"/>He will find a wound and disgrace,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and his shame will not be wiped out.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 6:33"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PRO 6:34"/>For jealousy is the heat of a man,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he will not spare in the day of vengeance.
<verse eid="PRO 6:34"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PRO 6:35"/>He will not lift up the face of any ransom,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he will not be willing if you increase the bribe.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 6:35"/><verse eid="PRO 6:35"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 6"/>
  <chapter number="7" style="c" sid="PRO 7"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 7:1"/>My son, keep my sayings
</para>
  <para style="q1">and store up my commandments with you.
<verse eid="PRO 7:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 7:2"/>Keep my commandments and live,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and my law, as the pupil of your eyes.
<verse eid="PRO 7:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 7:3"/>Tie them on your fingers;
</para>
  <para style="q1">write them on the tablet of your heart.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 7:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 7:4"/>Say to Wisdom, “You {are} my sister,”
</para>
  <para style="q1">and call to Understanding, “Kinsman,”
<verse eid="PRO 7:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 7:5"/>in order to keep you from the strange woman,
</para>
  <para style="q1">from the foreign woman who makes her sayings smooth.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 7:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 7:6"/>For at the window of my house,
</para>
  <para style="q1">through the window lattice, I looked down.
<verse eid="PRO 7:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 7:7"/>And I saw among the naive ones,
</para>
  <para style="q1">I discerned among the sons, a young man lacking of heart

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 7:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 7:8"/>passing through the lane beside her corner,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he steps {in} the way of her house,
<verse eid="PRO 7:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 7:9"/>in the twilight breeze, in the evening of day,
</para>
  <para style="q1">in the pupil of the night and darkness.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 7:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 7:10"/>And behold, {there is} a woman to meet him,
</para>
  <para style="q1">{with} the garment of a prostitute and guarded of heart.
<verse eid="PRO 7:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 7:11"/>(She {is} a loud and rebellious one;
</para>
  <para style="q1">her feet do not stay in her house.
<verse eid="PRO 7:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 7:12"/>At {one} time in the street, at {another} time in the open areas,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and beside every corner she lies in wait.)

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 7:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 7:13"/>And she grabs him and kisses him;
</para>
  <para style="q1">she strengthens her face and says to him,
<verse eid="PRO 7:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 7:14"/>“The sacrifices of peace offerings {are} with me;
</para>
  <para style="q1">today I paid my vows.
<verse eid="PRO 7:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 7:15"/>Therefore, I came out to meet you,
</para>
  <para style="q1">to diligently seek your face, and I found you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 7:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 7:16"/>I have spread my couch {with} coverings,
</para>
  <para style="q1">colored linen of Egypt.
<verse eid="PRO 7:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 7:17"/>I have sprinkled my bed
</para>
  <para style="q1">{with} myrrh, aloes, and cinnamon.
<verse eid="PRO 7:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 7:18"/>Come, let us drink fully of lovemaking until the morning;
</para>
  <para style="q1">let us delight ourselves with loves!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 7:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 7:19"/>For the man is not in his house;
</para>
  <para style="q1">he went on a road far away.
<verse eid="PRO 7:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 7:20"/>He took the bag of silver in his hand;
</para>
  <para style="q1">on the day of the full moon he will enter his house.”
<verse eid="PRO 7:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 7:21"/>She leads him astray with the abundance of her instruction;
</para>
  <para style="q1">with the smoothness of her lips she compels him.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 7:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 7:22"/>Following after her suddenly,
</para>
  <para style="q1">like an ox to slaughter he goes,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and like an ankle chain to the correction of a fool,
<verse eid="PRO 7:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 7:23"/>until an arrow splits his liver;
</para>
  <para style="q1">like a bird rushing into a trap,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he did not know that it {was} for his life.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 7:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 7:24"/>And now, sons, listen to me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and be attentive to the sayings of my mouth.
<verse eid="PRO 7:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 7:25"/>Do not let your heart turn aside to her ways;
</para>
  <para style="q1">do not wander into her tracks.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 7:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 7:26"/>For she has caused many pierced ones to fall,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and numerous {are} all her slain ones.
<verse eid="PRO 7:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 7:27"/>Her house {is} the ways of Sheol,
</para>
  <para style="q1">descending to the rooms of death.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 7:27"/><verse eid="PRO 7:27"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 7"/>
  <chapter number="8" style="c" sid="PRO 8"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 8:1"/>Does not Wisdom call out,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and Understanding give her voice?
<verse eid="PRO 8:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 8:2"/>At the head of the heights beside the road,
</para>
  <para style="q1">the house of the paths, she stations herself.
<verse eid="PRO 8:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 8:3"/>At the hand of the gates, at the mouth of the city,
</para>
  <para style="q1">the entrance of the openings, she cries out.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 8:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 8:4"/>“To you, men, I call,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and my voice {is} to the sons of man.
<verse eid="PRO 8:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 8:5"/>Understand prudence, naive ones,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and stupid ones, understand heart.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 8:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 8:6"/>Listen, for noble things I will speak,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the opening of my lips {will be} upright things.
<verse eid="PRO 8:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 8:7"/>For my palate will utter truth,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and wickedness {is} an abomination to my lips.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 8:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 8:8"/>All the words of my mouth {are} in righteousness;
</para>
  <para style="q1">there is nothing twisted or crooked in them.
<verse eid="PRO 8:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 8:9"/>All of them {are} straightforward things for the understanding one
</para>
  <para style="q1">and upright things for finders of knowledge.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 8:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 8:10"/>Take my instruction and not silver,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and knowledge rather than choice gold.
<verse eid="PRO 8:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 8:11"/>For wisdom {is} better than coral pearls,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and all desired things do not compare with her.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 8:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 8:12"/>I, Wisdom, I dwell with Prudence,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and knowledge of discretion I find.
<verse eid="PRO 8:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 8:13"/>The fear of Yahweh {is} to hate evil.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Pride and arrogance and the evil way and the mouth of perverse things I hate.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 8:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 8:14"/>Counsel and sound wisdom {are} mine;
</para>
  <para style="q1">I {am} understanding; strength {is} mine.
<verse eid="PRO 8:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 8:15"/>By me kings reign and dignitaries decree righteousness.
<verse eid="PRO 8:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 8:16"/>By me, princes rule,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and nobles, all judges of righteousness.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 8:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 8:17"/>I myself love those who love me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and those who diligently seek me will find me.
<verse eid="PRO 8:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 8:18"/>Riches and honor {are} with me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">lasting wealth and righteousness.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 8:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 8:19"/>My fruit {is} better than gold and than refined gold,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and my produce, than choice silver.
<verse eid="PRO 8:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 8:20"/>I walk in the path of righteousness,
</para>
  <para style="q1">in the midst of the pathways of justice,
<verse eid="PRO 8:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 8:21"/>to cause those who love me to inherit substance;
</para>
  <para style="q1">and their treasuries, I will fill.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 8:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 8:22"/>Yahweh possessed me {at} the beginning of his way,
</para>
  <para style="q1">before his works from then.
<verse eid="PRO 8:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 8:23"/>From eternity I was poured out,<note style="f" caller="+"> <char style="ft" closed="false">Instead of </char><char style="fqa" closed="true">was poured out</char>, some read the Hebrew word as <char style="fqa" closed="true">was shaped.</char></note>
</para>
  <para style="q1">from the head, from the ancient times of the earth.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 8:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 8:24"/>When there were no watery depths, I was brought forth,
</para>
  <para style="q1">when there were no springs heavy<note style="f" caller="+"> <char style="ft" closed="false">Instead of </char><char style="fqa" closed="true">heavy</char>, some versions read the Hebrew word as <char style="fqa" closed="true">overflowing.</char></note>
with water.
<verse eid="PRO 8:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 8:25"/>Before the mountains were sunk,
</para>
  <para style="q1">to the face of the hills, I was brought forth,

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 8:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 8:26"/>before he made the earth or the outside places
</para>
  <para style="q1">or the head of the loose soil of the world.
<verse eid="PRO 8:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 8:27"/>When he established the heavens, I {was} there,
</para>
  <para style="q1">when he inscribed a circle over the face of the watery deep,

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 8:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 8:28"/>when he made firm the clouds above,
</para>
  <para style="q1">when the springs of the watery deep became strong,
<verse eid="PRO 8:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 8:29"/>when he set up for the sea its statute,
</para>
  <para style="q1">so waters do not cross over his mouth,
</para>
  <para style="q1">when he inscribed the foundations of the earth.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 8:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 8:30"/>Then I was beside him {as} a skilled worker,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and I was a delight day {by} day,
</para>
  <para style="q1">frolicking before his face at every time.
<verse eid="PRO 8:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PRO 8:31"/>Frolicking in the world of his earth,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and my delights {were} with the sons of man.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 8:31"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PRO 8:32"/>And now, sons, listen to me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and happy {are} they {who} keep my ways.
<verse eid="PRO 8:32"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PRO 8:33"/>Hear instruction,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and be wise, and do not neglect {it}.
<verse eid="PRO 8:33"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PRO 8:34"/>Happy {is} the man listening to me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">keeping vigil over my doors day {by} day,
</para>
  <para style="q1">keeping watch {over} the doorposts of my entrances.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 8:34"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PRO 8:35"/>For a finder of me {is} a finder of life,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he obtains favor from Yahweh.
<verse eid="PRO 8:35"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="PRO 8:36"/>But a misser of me does violence to his life;
</para>
  <para style="q1">all haters of me love death.”

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 8:36"/><verse eid="PRO 8:36"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 8"/>
  <chapter number="9" style="c" sid="PRO 9"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 9:1"/>Wisdom has built her house;
</para>
  <para style="q1">she has hewn out her seven pillars.
<verse eid="PRO 9:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 9:2"/>She has slaughtered her slaughter, she has mixed her wine,
</para>
  <para style="q1">also she has arranged her table.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 9:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 9:3"/>She has sent out her young women;
</para>
  <para style="q1">she calls out on the tops of the heights of the city.
<verse eid="PRO 9:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 9:4"/>“Whoever {is} naive, let him turn aside here,”
</para>
  <para style="q1">she says to him lacking of heart.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 9:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 9:5"/>“Come, eat my bread,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and drink the wine I have mixed.
<verse eid="PRO 9:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 9:6"/>Forsake naive things and live;
</para>
  <para style="q1">and stride on the way of understanding.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 9:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 9:7"/>The instructor of a mocker receives disgrace for himself,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the rebuker of a wicked {one}, his injury.
<verse eid="PRO 9:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 9:8"/>Do not rebuke a mocker, lest he hate you;
</para>
  <para style="q1">rebuke a wise one, and he will love you.
<verse eid="PRO 9:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 9:9"/>Give to a wise {one}, and he will become more wise;
</para>
  <para style="q1">inform a righteous {one}, and he will increase learning.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 9:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 9:10"/>The beginning of wisdom {is} the fear of Yahweh
</para>
  <para style="q1">and knowledge of holy things {is} understanding.
<verse eid="PRO 9:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 9:11"/>Indeed, by me your days will increase,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and years of life will be added to you.
<verse eid="PRO 9:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 9:12"/>If you are wise, you are wise for yourself,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and {if} you mock, you alone will bear {it}.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 9:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 9:13"/>The woman of stupidity {is} loud,
</para>
  <para style="q1">naive, and she does not know anything.
<verse eid="PRO 9:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 9:14"/>And she sits at the opening of her house,
</para>
  <para style="q1">on a seat {by} the heights of the city,
<verse eid="PRO 9:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 9:15"/>to call to those who pass over the way,
</para>
  <para style="q1">the ones going straight {on} their paths.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 9:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 9:16"/>“Whoever {is} naive, let him turn aside here!”
</para>
  <para style="q1">And she says to him, the lacking of heart,
<verse eid="PRO 9:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 9:17"/>“Stolen waters are sweet,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and bread of secrecies is pleasant.”
<verse eid="PRO 9:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 9:18"/>But he does not know that the spirits of the dead {are} there;
</para>
  <para style="q1">in the depths of Sheol {are} her called ones.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 9:18"/><verse eid="PRO 9:18"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 9"/>
  <chapter number="10" style="c" sid="PRO 10"/>
  <para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 10:1"/>The proverbs of Solomon:
</para>
  <para style="q1">A wise son gladdens a father,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but a stupid son {is} the grief of his mother.
<verse eid="PRO 10:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 10:2"/>Treasures of wickedness do not profit,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but righteousness delivers from death.
<verse eid="PRO 10:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 10:3"/>Yahweh does not let the life of the righteous starve,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the desire of the wicked he thrusts away.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 10:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 10:4"/>A palm of idleness makes poverty,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the hand of the diligent ones makes rich.
<verse eid="PRO 10:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 10:5"/>One who gathers in the summer {is} a son who has insight,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but one who sleeps in the harvest {is} a son who acts shamefully.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 10:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 10:6"/>Blessings {are} for the head of the righteous,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the mouth of the wicked covers violence.
<verse eid="PRO 10:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 10:7"/>The memory of the righteous one {is} for a blessing,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the name of the wicked ones will rot.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 10:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 10:8"/>The one wise of heart receives commands,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the one stupid of lips will be thrown down.
<verse eid="PRO 10:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 10:9"/>One who walks with integrity will walk securely,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but one who causes his ways to be crooked will be known.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 10:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 10:10"/>One who winks an eye gives pain,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the one foolish of lips will be thrown down.

<verse eid="PRO 10:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 10:11"/>A fountain of life {is} the mouth of the righteous one,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the mouth of the wicked ones covers violence.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 10:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 10:12"/>Hatred stirs up quarrels,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but love covers over all transgressions.
<verse eid="PRO 10:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 10:13"/>On the lips of the discerning one, wisdom is found,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but a rod {is} for the back of the one lacking of heart.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 10:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 10:14"/>Wise ones store up knowledge,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the mouth of a fool {is} near ruin.
<verse eid="PRO 10:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 10:15"/>The wealth of the rich one {is} the city of his strength;
</para>
  <para style="q1">the ruin of lowly ones {is} their poverty.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 10:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 10:16"/>The wage of a righteous {one} {is} to life;
</para>
  <para style="q1">the income of a wicked {one} {is} to sin.
<verse eid="PRO 10:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 10:17"/>{On} a path to life {is} one who keeps instruction,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but one who forsakes rebuke goes astray.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 10:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 10:18"/>One who covers hate {has} lips of falsehood,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and one who causes an evil report to go forth, he {is} a stupid one.
<verse eid="PRO 10:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 10:19"/>With a multitude of words, transgression does not cease,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but one who restrains his lips is insightful.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 10:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 10:20"/>Choice silver {is} the tongue of the righteous one;
</para>
  <para style="q1">the heart of the wicked ones {is} like little.
<verse eid="PRO 10:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 10:21"/>The lips of the righteous one shepherd many,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but fools die by lack of heart.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 10:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 10:22"/>The blessing of Yahweh, it causes riches,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and striving does not add {more} with it.
<verse eid="PRO 10:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 10:23"/>Like laughter for a stupid one {is} doing a wicked plan,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but wisdom, for a man of understanding.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 10:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 10:24"/>The terror of the wicked one, it will come to him,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the desire of the righteous ones will be given.
<verse eid="PRO 10:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 10:25"/>When a whirlwind passes over, then there is no {more} wicked,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but a righteous one {is} a foundation of eternity.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 10:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 10:26"/>Like vinegar to the teeth and smoke to the eyes,
</para>
  <para style="q1">so {is} the lazy one to one who sends him.
<verse eid="PRO 10:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 10:27"/>The fear of Yahweh will add days,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the years of the wicked ones will be short.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 10:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 10:28"/>The hope of the righteous ones {is} joy,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the expectation of the wicked ones will perish.
<verse eid="PRO 10:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 10:29"/>A stronghold for the one with integrity {is} the way of Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but ruin for doers of iniquity.
<verse eid="PRO 10:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 10:30"/>A righteous one will not falter to eternity,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but wicked ones will not dwell {in} the land.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 10:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PRO 10:31"/>The mouth of the righteous one bears the fruit of wisdom,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the tongue of the perverse ones will be cut off.
<verse eid="PRO 10:31"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PRO 10:32"/>The lips of the righteous one know favor,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the mouth of the wicked ones, perverse things.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 10:32"/><verse eid="PRO 10:32"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 10"/>
  <chapter number="11" style="c" sid="PRO 11"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 11:1"/>Scales of deceit {are} an abomination to Yahweh
</para>
  <para style="q1">but a whole stone {is} his delight.
<verse eid="PRO 11:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 11:2"/>When presumptuousness comes, then disgrace comes,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but with modest ones {is} wisdom.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 11:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 11:3"/>The integrity of the upright ones will guide them,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the crookedness of the treacherous ones will destroy them.
<verse eid="PRO 11:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 11:4"/>Wealth will not profit in the day of rage,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but righteousness will deliver from death.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 11:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 11:5"/>The righteousness of a blameless one will make his way straight,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but by his wickedness, a wicked one will fall.
<verse eid="PRO 11:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 11:6"/>The righteousness of the upright will deliver them,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but by the desire of treacherous {ones} they will be captured.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 11:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 11:7"/>At the death of a wicked man expectation will perish,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the hope of strength perishes.
<verse eid="PRO 11:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 11:8"/>A righteous {one} is drawn away from distress,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and a wicked {one} enters instead of him.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 11:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 11:9"/>With a mouth a godless {one} destroys his neighbor,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but with knowledge, the righteous will be delivered.
<verse eid="PRO 11:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 11:10"/>In the good of the righteous a city exults;
</para>
  <para style="q1">and when the wicked perish, a shout of joy.
<verse eid="PRO 11:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 11:11"/>With the blessing of the upright a city is raised up,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but with the mouth of the wicked it is torn down.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 11:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 11:12"/>One despising his neighbor {is} lacking of heart,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but a man of understandings will keep quiet.
<verse eid="PRO 11:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 11:13"/>One going about {with} gossip uncovers a secret,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but one faithful of spirit covers a matter.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 11:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 11:14"/>When there are no directions, a people falls,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but salvation {is} in an abundance of counsel.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 11:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 11:15"/>One will be harmed {with} harm if he pledges for a stranger,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but one hating hand clasps {is} secure.
<verse eid="PRO 11:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 11:16"/>A woman of grace will grasp honor,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the ruthless will grasp riches.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 11:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 11:17"/>A man of covenant faithfulness repays his soul,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but a cruel {one} troubles his flesh.
<verse eid="PRO 11:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 11:18"/>A wicked {one} makes a wage of falsehood,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but {one} sowing righteousness, a wage of truth.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 11:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 11:19"/>True righteousness {is} to life,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but one who pursues evil {is} to his death.
<verse eid="PRO 11:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 11:20"/>An abomination to Yahweh {is} the crooked of heart,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but his delight {is} the blameless of way.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 11:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 11:21"/>Hand to hand, a wicked {one} will not remain blameless,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the seed of the righteous will safely escape.
<verse eid="PRO 11:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 11:22"/>A ring of gold in the nose of a pig
</para>
  <para style="q1">{is} a beautiful woman turning away {from} discretion.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 11:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 11:23"/>The desire of the righteous {is} only good;
</para>
  <para style="q1">the expectation of the wicked {is} rage.
<verse eid="PRO 11:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 11:24"/>There is a scatterer yet being added to more,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and {one} withholding more than {what is} right,
</para>
  <para style="q1">yet to poverty.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 11:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 11:25"/>A life of blessing will be fattened,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the one who drenches, he also will be drenched.
<verse eid="PRO 11:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 11:26"/>One withholding grain, people will curse him,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but a blessing {is} for the head of the seller.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 11:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 11:27"/>One diligently seeking good seeks favor,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but one searching {for} evil, it will come {to} him.
<verse eid="PRO 11:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 11:28"/>One trusting in his riches, he himself will fall,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but like a leaf, the righteous will sprout.

<verse eid="PRO 11:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 11:29"/>One troubling his house will inherit wind,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and a fool {will be} a slave to the wise of heart.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 11:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 11:30"/>The fruit of the righteous {is} a tree of life,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and one taking souls is wise.
<verse eid="PRO 11:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PRO 11:31"/>Behold, a righteous {one} in the land will be repaid,
</para>
  <para style="q1">how much more a wicked {one} and a sinner!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 11:31"/><verse eid="PRO 11:31"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 11"/>
  <chapter number="12" style="c" sid="PRO 12"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 12:1"/>The lover of correction loves knowledge,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the hater of rebuke {is} stupid.
<verse eid="PRO 12:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 12:2"/>A good one obtains favor from Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but a man of schemes he will condemn.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 12:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 12:3"/>A man will not be established by wickedness,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the root of the righteous will not be shaken.
<verse eid="PRO 12:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 12:4"/>A wife of worth {is} the crown of her husband,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but she who causes shame {is} like rottenness in his bones.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 12:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 12:5"/>The plans of the righteous {are} justice;
</para>
  <para style="q1">the directions of the wicked {are} deceit.
<verse eid="PRO 12:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 12:6"/>The words of the wicked lie in wait {for} blood,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the mouth of the upright will deliver them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 12:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 12:7"/>The wicked are overthrown, and they are naught,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the house of the righteous will stand.
<verse eid="PRO 12:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 12:8"/>For the mouth of his insight a man will be praised,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but {one} twisted of heart will be for contempt.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 12:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 12:9"/>Better {is} being disregarded and having a servant
</para>
  <para style="q1">than honoring oneself and lacking bread.
<verse eid="PRO 12:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 12:10"/>A righteous {one} knows the life of his animal,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the compassion of the wicked {is} cruel.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 12:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 12:11"/>Bread will satisfy one who works his ground,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but one who pursues empty things {is} lacking of heart.
<verse eid="PRO 12:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 12:12"/>A wicked {one} desires the snare of the evil,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the root of the righteous will give.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 12:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 12:13"/>In the transgression of lips {is} the snare of an evil {one},
</para>
  <para style="q1">but a righteous {one} will go out from distress.
<verse eid="PRO 12:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 12:14"/>From the fruit of the mouth of a man will he be satisfied {with} good,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the accomplishment of the hands of a man will return to him.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 12:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 12:15"/>The way of a fool {is} right in his eyes,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but a wise one listens to counsel.
<verse eid="PRO 12:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 12:16"/>A fool—his anger is known on the day,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but a prudent one covers dishonor.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 12:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 12:17"/>He who breathes out faithfulness tells righteousness,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but a witness of falsehoods, deceit.
<verse eid="PRO 12:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 12:18"/>There is one speaking thoughtlessly like the thrusts of a sword,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the tongue of the wise ones—healing.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 12:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 12:19"/>A lip of truth will be established to perpetuity,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but a tongue of falsehood as long as I would blink.
<verse eid="PRO 12:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 12:20"/>Deceit {is} in the heart of devisers of evil,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but joy {is} for advisers of peace.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 12:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 12:21"/>Any iniquity will not be allowed to happen to the righteous,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the wicked are full of evil.
<verse eid="PRO 12:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 12:22"/>An abomination to Yahweh {are} lips of falsehood,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but doers of faithfulness {are} his delight.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 12:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 12:23"/>A prudent man covers knowledge,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the heart of the stupid calls out folly.
<verse eid="PRO 12:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 12:24"/>The hand of the diligent will rule,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but an idle one will become a forced laborer.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 12:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 12:25"/>Concern in the heart of a man weighs it down,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but a good word gladdens it.
<verse eid="PRO 12:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 12:26"/>A righteous {one} searches out from his neighbor,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the way of the wicked leads them astray.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 12:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 12:27"/>A negligent one will not roast his game,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the wealth of a man {is} precious {for} a diligent one.
<verse eid="PRO 12:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 12:28"/>In the path of righteousness {is} life,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the way of the beaten path {is} no death.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 12:28"/><verse eid="PRO 12:28"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 12"/>
  <chapter number="13" style="c" sid="PRO 13"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 13:1"/>A wise son, the instruction of a father,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but a mocking {one} does not listen to rebuke.
<verse eid="PRO 13:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 13:2"/>From the fruit of the mouth of a man he eats good,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the appetite of the treacherous ones, violence.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 13:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 13:3"/>One guarding his mouth keeps his life;
</para>
  <para style="q1">one opening his lips, ruin for him.
<verse eid="PRO 13:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 13:4"/>A lazy one, his appetite is craving and there is nothing,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the appetite of the diligent will be fattened.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 13:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 13:5"/>A righteous {one} hates a word of falsehood,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but a wicked {one} causes a stink and causes embarrassment.
<verse eid="PRO 13:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 13:6"/>Righteousness guards the blameless of way,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but wickedness leads a sinful one astray.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 13:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 13:7"/>There is one pretending to be rich, but there is nothing {at} all;
</para>
  <para style="q1">one pretending to be poor, but much wealth.
<verse eid="PRO 13:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 13:8"/>The ransom of the life of a man {is} his riches,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but a poor one does not hear a rebuke.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 13:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 13:9"/>The light of the righteous will be glad,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the lamp of the wicked goes out.
<verse eid="PRO 13:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 13:10"/>With presumptuousness comes only contention,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but with those who are counseled, wisdom.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 13:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 13:11"/>Wealth from emptiness will dwindle,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but one gathering by hand will increase.
<verse eid="PRO 13:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 13:12"/>Hope deferred makes a heart sick,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but a desire fulfilled {is} a tree of life.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 13:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 13:13"/>One despising a word, it will go badly for him,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but {one} fearing a command, that one will be rewarded.

<verse eid="PRO 13:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 13:14"/>The law of the wise {is} a fountain of life,
</para>
  <para style="q1">to turn away from the snares of death.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 13:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 13:15"/>Good insight gives favor,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the way of treacherous ones {is} permanent.
<verse eid="PRO 13:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 13:16"/>Every prudent {one} acts with knowledge,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but a stupid person displays folly.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 13:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 13:17"/>A wicked messenger falls into evil,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but an envoy of faithfulness {causes} healing.
<verse eid="PRO 13:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 13:18"/>Poverty and shame {are for} one avoiding correction,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but one keeping a rebuke will be honored.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 13:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 13:19"/>A desire {that} occurs will be pleasing to the self,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the abomination of the stupid {is} turning away from evil.
<verse eid="PRO 13:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 13:20"/>One walking with wise ones will become wise,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but one associating with stupid ones will be harmed.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 13:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 13:21"/>Evil will pursue the sinful,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but goodness will reward the righteous.
<verse eid="PRO 13:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 13:22"/>The good will cause sons of sons to inherit,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the wealth of a sinner is stored up for the righteous.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 13:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 13:23"/>Much food {is in} the unplowed field of poor ones,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but there is {food} being swept away by no justice.
<verse eid="PRO 13:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 13:24"/>One who withholds his rod hates his son,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but one who loves him diligently seeks him {with} discipline.

<verse eid="PRO 13:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 13:25"/>A righteous {one} eating to the satisfaction of his appetite,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the stomach of the wicked will lack.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 13:25"/><verse eid="PRO 13:25"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 13"/>
  <chapter number="14" style="c" sid="PRO 14"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 14:1"/>The wisest of women builds her house,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but a foolish woman tears it down with her hands.
<verse eid="PRO 14:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 14:2"/>The one walking in his uprightness fears Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the one crooked in his ways despises him.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 14:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 14:3"/>In the mouth of a fool {is} a rod of pride,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the lips of the wise ones will preserve them.
<verse eid="PRO 14:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 14:4"/>Where there are no cattle {is} a trough of cleanness,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but an abundance of produce {is} by the strength of an ox.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 14:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 14:5"/>A witness of faithfulness will not lie,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but a witness of falsehood breathes out lies.
<verse eid="PRO 14:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 14:6"/>A mocker seeks wisdom and there is none,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but knowledge is easy for the understanding one.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 14:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 14:7"/>Go before a man of stupidity,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and you will not know lips of knowledge.
<verse eid="PRO 14:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 14:8"/>The wisdom of a prudent {one} is to understand his way,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the folly of the stupid {is} deceit.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 14:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 14:9"/>The foolish mock the guilt offering,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but among the upright {is} favor.
<verse eid="PRO 14:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 14:10"/>A heart knows the bitterness of itself,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and in its joy a stranger will not share.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 14:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 14:11"/>The house of the wicked will be destroyed,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the tent of the upright will flourish.
<verse eid="PRO 14:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 14:12"/>There is a straight road to the face of a man,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but its end {is} the ways of death.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 14:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 14:13"/>Even in laughter a heart may ache,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the end of joy {may be} grief.
<verse eid="PRO 14:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 14:14"/>A backsliding heart will be filled from his ways,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but a good man, from his deeds.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 14:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 14:15"/>A naive one believes every word,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but a prudent {one} considers his step.
<verse eid="PRO 14:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 14:16"/>A wise {one} fears and turns away from trouble,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but a stupid {one} interferes and is confident.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 14:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 14:17"/>{One} short of nostrils does folly,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and a man of schemes is hated.
<verse eid="PRO 14:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 14:18"/>Simpletons inherit folly,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the prudent will wear a crown of knowledge.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 14:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 14:19"/>The evil will bow down to the face of the good,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the wicked at the gates of the righteous one.
<verse eid="PRO 14:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 14:20"/>One who is poor is hated even by his neighbor,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but those who love the rich {are} many.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 14:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 14:21"/>The one despising his neighbor sins,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the one who shows favor to the lowly, happy {is} he.
<verse eid="PRO 14:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 14:22"/>Do not devisers of evil go astray?
</para>
  <para style="q1">But covenant faithfulness and trustworthiness {are} devisers of good.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 14:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 14:23"/>With all toil is profit,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the word of lips {is} only for lack.
<verse eid="PRO 14:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 14:24"/>The crown of the wise ones {is} their riches;
</para>
  <para style="q1">the folly of stupid ones {is} folly.

<verse eid="PRO 14:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 14:25"/>A witness of truth rescues lives,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but a fraud breathes out lies.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 14:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 14:26"/>In the fear of Yahweh {is} strong confidence,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and for his sons he will be a refuge.
<verse eid="PRO 14:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 14:27"/>The fear of Yahweh {is} a fountain of life,
</para>
  <para style="q1">to turn away from the snares of death.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 14:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 14:28"/>With the abundance of people {is} the majesty of a king,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but with the end of the population {comes} the ruin of the ruler.
<verse eid="PRO 14:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 14:29"/>One long of nostrils {is} abundant {in} understanding,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but one short of spirit lifts up folly.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 14:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 14:30"/>A heart of healing {is} life to bodies,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but envy {is} the decay of bones.
<verse eid="PRO 14:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PRO 14:31"/>An oppressor of a lowly one taunts his maker,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but one showing favor to a needy one honors him.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 14:31"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PRO 14:32"/>By his evil the wicked {one} is thrust down,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the righteous {one} finds refuge in his death.
<verse eid="PRO 14:32"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PRO 14:33"/>In the heart of the understanding one rests wisdom,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and in the midst of the stupid she will be known.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 14:33"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PRO 14:34"/>Righteousness raises a nation,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but sin {is} shame for peoples.
<verse eid="PRO 14:34"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PRO 14:35"/>The delight of a king {is} for the servant who has insight,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but his rage is {for} one who acts shamefully.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 14:35"/><verse eid="PRO 14:35"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 14"/>
  <chapter number="15" style="c" sid="PRO 15"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 15:1"/>A gentle answer turns back heat,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but a word of pain lifts up a nose.
<verse eid="PRO 15:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 15:2"/>The tongue of the wise makes knowledge good,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the mouth of the stupid gushes forth folly.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 15:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 15:3"/>The eyes of Yahweh {are} in every place,
</para>
  <para style="q1">watching the evil and the good.
<verse eid="PRO 15:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 15:4"/>A healing tongue {is} a tree of life,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but crookedness in it {is} a breaking in the spirit.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 15:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 15:5"/>A fool despises the correction of his father,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but one who keeps rebuke is prudent.
<verse eid="PRO 15:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 15:6"/>The house of the righteous {has} much treasure,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but in the harvest of the wicked is being troubled.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 15:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 15:7"/>The lips of the wise scatter knowledge,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the heart of the stupid {is} not so.
<verse eid="PRO 15:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 15:8"/>The sacrifice of the wicked {is} an abomination to Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the prayer of the upright {is} his delight.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 15:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 15:9"/>An abomination to Yahweh {is} the way of the wicked,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but a pursuer of righteousness he loves.
<verse eid="PRO 15:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 15:10"/>Severe discipline {is} for one who forsakes the path;
</para>
  <para style="q1">one who hates rebuke will die.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 15:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 15:11"/>Sheol and Abaddon {are} before Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q1">how much more the hearts of the sons of man!
<verse eid="PRO 15:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 15:12"/>A mocker does not love one who rebukes him;
</para>
  <para style="q1">to the wise, he will not go.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 15:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 15:13"/>A joyful heart makes a face glad,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but by pain of heart, a spirit {is} stricken.
<verse eid="PRO 15:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 15:14"/>The heart of the understanding one seeks knowledge,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the mouth of the stupid feeds on folly.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 15:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 15:15"/>All the days of the afflicted {are} evil,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the good of heart {has} a feast continually.
<verse eid="PRO 15:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 15:16"/>Better {is} a little with the fear of Yahweh
</para>
  <para style="q1">than much treasure and anxiety with it.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 15:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 15:17"/>Better {is} a portion of vegetables and love there
</para>
  <para style="q1">than a fattened ox and hatred with it.
<verse eid="PRO 15:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 15:18"/>A man of heat stirs up a quarrel,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but one long of nostrils will quiet a dispute.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 15:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 15:19"/>The way of the lazy {is} like a hedge of briar,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the path of the upright {is} a built-up highway.
<verse eid="PRO 15:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 15:20"/>A wise son gladdens a father,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but a stupid man despises his mother.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 15:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 15:21"/>Folly {is} a joy to the lacking of heart,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the man of understanding makes to go straight.
<verse eid="PRO 15:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 15:22"/>Plans are broken with no counsel,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but with a multitude of advisers, it will stand.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 15:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 15:23"/>Joy {is} for the man in the answer of his mouth,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and how good {is} a word in its time.
<verse eid="PRO 15:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 15:24"/>The path of life {is} upward for the insightful one,
</para>
  <para style="q1">in order to turn away from Sheol below.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 15:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 15:25"/>Yahweh will tear down the house of the proud,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but he will set up the boundary of the widow.
<verse eid="PRO 15:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 15:26"/>Evil thoughts {are} an abomination to Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but words of pleasantness {are} pure ones.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 15:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 15:27"/>One who unjustly gains unjust gain troubles his house,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but one who hates bribes will live.
<verse eid="PRO 15:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 15:28"/>The heart of the righteous considers {how} to answer,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the mouth of the wicked gushes forth evils.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 15:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 15:29"/>Yahweh {is} far from the wicked,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the prayer of the righteous, he hears.
<verse eid="PRO 15:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 15:30"/>The luminary of the eyes gladdens the heart;
</para>
  <para style="q1">good news fattens the bone.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 15:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PRO 15:31"/>An ear hearing the rebuke of life
</para>
  <para style="q1">will lodge in the midst of the wise ones.
<verse eid="PRO 15:31"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PRO 15:32"/>One who avoids correction rejects his life,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but one who hears rebuke acquires heart.

<verse eid="PRO 15:32"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PRO 15:33"/>The fear of Yahweh {is} instruction of wisdom,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and to the face of honor {is} humility.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 15:33"/><verse eid="PRO 15:33"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 15"/>
  <chapter number="16" style="c" sid="PRO 16"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 16:1"/>The arrangements of the heart {are} a man’s,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the answer of the tongue {is} from Yahweh.
<verse eid="PRO 16:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 16:2"/>All the ways of a man {are} pure in his eyes,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but Yahweh examines spirits.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 16:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 16:3"/>Roll to Yahweh your works,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and your plans will be established.
<verse eid="PRO 16:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 16:4"/>Yahweh has made all for its purpose
</para>
  <para style="q1">and even a wicked {one} for the day of evil.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 16:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 16:5"/>An abomination to Yahweh {is} each one high of heart,
</para>
  <para style="q1">hand to hand he will not remain blameless.
<verse eid="PRO 16:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 16:6"/>By covenant faithfulness and trustworthiness, iniquity is atoned {for},
</para>
  <para style="q1">and by the fear of Yahweh, one turns away from evil.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 16:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 16:7"/>When Yahweh is pleased with the ways of a man,
</para>
  <para style="q1">he causes even his enemies to be at peace with him.
<verse eid="PRO 16:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 16:8"/>Better {is} a little with righteousness
</para>
  <para style="q1">than an abundance of produce with no justice.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 16:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 16:9"/>The heart of a man plans his way,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but Yahweh establishes his step.
<verse eid="PRO 16:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 16:10"/>Divination {is} on the lips of a king,
</para>
  <para style="q1">in judgment, his mouth must not act unfaithfully.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 16:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 16:11"/>A scale with the two balances of justice {belong} to Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q1">all the stones of the bag {are} his work.
<verse eid="PRO 16:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 16:12"/>An abomination of kings {is} doing wickedness,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for by righteousness is a throne established.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 16:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 16:13"/>The delight of kings {is} lips of righteousness,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he loves one who speaks upright things.
<verse eid="PRO 16:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 16:14"/>The heat of a king {is} messengers of death,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but a wise man will atone {for} it.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 16:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 16:15"/>In the light of the face of the king {is} life,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and his favor {is} like a cloud of spring rain.
<verse eid="PRO 16:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 16:16"/>How much better {it is} to acquire wisdom than gold,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and to acquire understanding is to be chosen {more} than silver.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 16:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 16:17"/>The highway of the upright ones turns away from evil;
</para>
  <para style="q1">one who protects his life guards his way.
<verse eid="PRO 16:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 16:18"/>To the face of a breaking {is} pride,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and to the face of a stumbling {is} a height of spirit.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 16:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 16:19"/>Better to be lowly of spirit {with} afflicted ones
</para>
  <para style="q1">than to share a portion {of} spoil {with} proud ones.
<verse eid="PRO 16:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 16:20"/>One who comprehends concerning a matter will find good,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and one who trusts in Yahweh, he {is} happy.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 16:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 16:21"/>The wise of heart will be called an understanding one,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the sweetness of lips increases learning.
<verse eid="PRO 16:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 16:22"/>A fountain of life {is} the insight of its owner,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the instruction of fools {is} folly.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 16:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 16:23"/>The heart of the wise makes his mouth insightful,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and on his lips it increases learning.
<verse eid="PRO 16:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 16:24"/>Words of pleasantness {are} a honeycomb of honey,
</para>
  <para style="q1">sweet to the soul and healing to the bone.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 16:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 16:25"/>There is a straight road to the face of a man
</para>
  <para style="q1">but its end {is} the ways of death.
<verse eid="PRO 16:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 16:26"/>The appetite of the laborer labors for him,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for his mouth presses on him.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 16:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 16:27"/>A man of worthlessness digs up evil
</para>
  <para style="q1">and on his lips {it is} like a scorching fire.
<verse eid="PRO 16:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 16:28"/>A man of perverse things lets loose strife,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and a murmurer separates the friendly.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 16:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 16:29"/>A man of violence entices his neighbor,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he leads him on a road {that is} not good.
<verse eid="PRO 16:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 16:30"/>One who shuts his eyes plans perverse things;
</para>
  <para style="q1">one who compresses his lips brings evil to completion.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 16:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PRO 16:31"/>Gray hair {is} a crown of splendor;
</para>
  <para style="q1">on the road of righteousness it is found.
<verse eid="PRO 16:31"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PRO 16:32"/>Better {is} one long of nostrils than a mighty one,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and one ruling his spirit than one capturing a city.

<verse eid="PRO 16:32"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PRO 16:33"/>Into the lap a lot is cast,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but its every judgment {is} from Yahweh.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 16:33"/><verse eid="PRO 16:33"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 16"/>
  <chapter number="17" style="c" sid="PRO 17"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 17:1"/>Better {is} a dry morsel and ease with it
</para>
  <para style="q1">than a house full of sacrifices of quarreling.
<verse eid="PRO 17:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 17:2"/>An insightful servant will rule over a shameful son,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and in the midst of brothers, he will share an inheritance.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 17:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 17:3"/>The smelting-pot {is} for the silver and the furnace {is} for the gold,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and Yahweh tests hearts.
<verse eid="PRO 17:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 17:4"/>The evildoer listens attentively to the lips of iniquity;
</para>
  <para style="q1">a liar gives ear to a tongue of destruction.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 17:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 17:5"/>A mocker of one who is poor taunts his maker;
</para>
  <para style="q1">one glad at calamity will not remain blameless.
<verse eid="PRO 17:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 17:6"/>The crown of the old {is} sons of sons,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the splendor of sons {is} their fathers.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 17:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 17:7"/>A lip of excess {is} not suitable for a worthless {one};
</para>
  <para style="q1">how much less a lip of falsehood for a noble.
<verse eid="PRO 17:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 17:8"/>A stone of favor {is} a bribe in the eyes of its owner;
</para>
  <para style="q1">he succeeds to all that he turns.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 17:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 17:9"/>One who covers a transgression seeks love,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but one who repeats a matter separates a close friend.
<verse eid="PRO 17:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 17:10"/>A rebuke goes down into an understanding one
</para>
  <para style="q1">more than striking a stupid one a hundred {times}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 17:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 17:11"/>An evil one seeks only rebellion,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and a cruel messenger will be sent against him.
<verse eid="PRO 17:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 17:12"/>Let a female bear robbed of offspring meet a man
</para>
  <para style="q1">and not a stupid one in his folly!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 17:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 17:13"/>One who returns evil for good,
</para>
  <para style="q1">evil will not depart from his house.
<verse eid="PRO 17:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 17:14"/>The beginning of a quarrel {is} the releasing of water,
</para>
  <para style="q1">so leave the dispute before it breaks out.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 17:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 17:15"/>One who declares a wicked one righteous
</para>
  <para style="q1">and one who declares a righteous one wicked,
</para>
  <para style="q1">even the two of them {are} an abomination to Yahweh.
<verse eid="PRO 17:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 17:16"/>Why {is} this: A payment {is} in the hand of a stupid one
</para>
  <para style="q1">to acquire wisdom, but there is no heart?

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 17:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 17:17"/>At every time the friend loves,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and a brother is born for distress.
<verse eid="PRO 17:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 17:18"/>A man lacking of heart {is} one who clasps a palm,
</para>
  <para style="q1">pledging a pledge to the face of his neighbor.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 17:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 17:19"/>One who loves transgression loves contention;
</para>
  <para style="q1">one who makes his opening high seeks a breaking.
<verse eid="PRO 17:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 17:20"/>One crooked of heart will not find goodness,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and one who is turned away in his tongue will fall into evil.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 17:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 17:21"/>One who begets a stupid one, {it is} for grief for him,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the father of a worthless one will not rejoice.
<verse eid="PRO 17:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 17:22"/>A joyful heart makes healing good,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but a broken spirit dries up bone.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 17:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 17:23"/>A wicked one takes a bribe from the bosom
</para>
  <para style="q1">to bend the paths of justice.
<verse eid="PRO 17:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 17:24"/>Wisdom {is} with the face of an understanding one,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the eyes of a stupid one {are} at the end of the earth.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 17:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 17:25"/>A stupid son {is} a grief to his father
</para>
  <para style="q1">and bitterness to her who bore him.
<verse eid="PRO 17:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 17:26"/>Actually to fine the righteous {is} not good;
</para>
  <para style="q1">to strike nobles {is} against uprightness.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 17:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 17:27"/>One restraining his words {is} one knowing knowledge,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the cool of spirit {is} a man of understanding.
<verse eid="PRO 17:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 17:28"/>Even a fool keeping silent will be considered wise;
</para>
  <para style="q1">one shutting his lips—understanding.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 17:28"/><verse eid="PRO 17:28"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 17"/>
  <chapter number="18" style="c" sid="PRO 18"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 18:1"/>One who separates himself seeks for desire;
</para>
  <para style="q1">against all sound wisdom, he breaks out.
<verse eid="PRO 18:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 18:2"/>A stupid one does not delight in understanding
</para>
  <para style="q1">but rather in his heart revealing itself.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 18:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 18:3"/>When a wicked one comes, contempt also comes,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and with shame, reproach.
<verse eid="PRO 18:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 18:4"/>The words of the mouth of a man {are} deep waters;
</para>
  <para style="q1">a fountain of wisdom {is} a gushing stream.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 18:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 18:5"/>{It is} not good to lift the face of the wicked,
</para>
  <para style="q1">to turn aside the righteous in the judgment.
<verse eid="PRO 18:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 18:6"/>The lips of a stupid one enter into a dispute,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and his mouth calls for blows.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 18:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 18:7"/>The mouth of a stupid one {is} ruin for him,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and his lips {are} a snare of his life.
<verse eid="PRO 18:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 18:8"/>The words of a murmurer {are} like things swallowed greedily,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and they themselves go down into the rooms of the belly.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 18:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 18:9"/>Also, one who slacks in his work,
</para>
  <para style="q1">he {is} a brother to an owner of destruction.
<verse eid="PRO 18:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 18:10"/>The name of Yahweh {is} a tower of strength;
</para>
  <para style="q1">the righteous {one} runs into it and is set on high.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 18:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 18:11"/>The wealth of the rich one {is} the city of his strength
</para>
  <para style="q1">and like a wall set on high—in his imagination.
<verse eid="PRO 18:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 18:12"/>To the face of breaking, the heart of a man is exalted,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but to the face of honor—humility.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 18:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 18:13"/>One who returns a word before he listens,
</para>
  <para style="q1">it {is} folly to him and shame.
<verse eid="PRO 18:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 18:14"/>The spirit of a man will endure his illness,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but a crushed spirit, who can lift it?

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 18:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 18:15"/>The heart of an understanding one acquires knowledge,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the ear of the wise seeks knowledge.
<verse eid="PRO 18:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 18:16"/>The gift of a man will make room for him,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and before the face of great ones it will guide him.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 18:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 18:17"/>The first one with his case {is} right;
</para>
  <para style="q1">then his neighbor comes and examines him.
<verse eid="PRO 18:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 18:18"/>The lot causes quarrels to cease,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and between mighty ones, it makes a separation.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 18:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 18:19"/>A brother offended {is} more than a city of strength,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and quarrels {are} like the gate bar of a fortress.
<verse eid="PRO 18:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 18:20"/>From the fruit of the mouth of a man his belly is satisfied;
</para>
  <para style="q1">{with} the produce of his lips, he is satisfied.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 18:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 18:21"/>Death and life {are} in the hand of the tongue,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and those who love it will eat its fruit.
<verse eid="PRO 18:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 18:22"/>He who finds a wife finds good,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he obtains favor from Yahweh.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 18:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 18:23"/>One who is poor speaks pleas,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but a rich one answers harshly.
<verse eid="PRO 18:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 18:24"/>A man of companions {is} to be broken,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but there is one who loves, clinging more than a brother.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 18:24"/><verse eid="PRO 18:24"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 18"/>
  <chapter number="19" style="c" sid="PRO 19"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 19:1"/>Better {is} one who is poor who walks in his integrity
</para>
  <para style="q1">than one who is crooked {in} his lips and he {is} a stupid one.
<verse eid="PRO 19:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 19:2"/>Also, zeal with no knowledge {is} not good,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and one who hurries with feet misses {the way}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 19:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 19:3"/>The folly of a man will lead astray his way,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and his heart will rage against Yahweh.
<verse eid="PRO 19:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 19:4"/>Wealth adds many companions,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but a lowly one is separated from his companions.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 19:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 19:5"/>A witness of falsehoods will not be blameless,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he who breathes out lies will not escape.
<verse eid="PRO 19:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 19:6"/>Many will entreat the face of a noble,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and everyone {is} the friend of a man of gift.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 19:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 19:7"/>All the brothers of one who is poor hate him;
</para>
  <para style="q1">how much more do his friends go far away from him!
</para>
  <para style="q1">He pursues {with} words; they {are} not.
<verse eid="PRO 19:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 19:8"/>The one acquiring heart is loving his life;
</para>
  <para style="q1">the one keeping understanding {is} to find good {fortune}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 19:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 19:9"/>A witness of falsehoods will not be blameless,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and one who breathes out lies will perish.
<verse eid="PRO 19:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 19:10"/>Luxury {is} not suitable for a stupid one;
</para>
  <para style="q1">how much less for a slave to rule over princes!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 19:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 19:11"/>The insight of a man makes his nose long,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and his splendor {is} to pass over a transgression.
<verse eid="PRO 19:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 19:12"/>The rage of a king {is} a growling like the young lion,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but his favor {is} like dew on vegetation.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 19:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 19:13"/>A stupid son {is} destruction to his father,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and a continual dripping, the quarrels of a wife.
<verse eid="PRO 19:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 19:14"/>A house and wealth {are} the inheritance of fathers,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but from Yahweh {is} a wife who has insight.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 19:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 19:15"/>Laziness causes deep sleep to fall,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and a life of idleness is hungry.
<verse eid="PRO 19:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 19:16"/>One who keeps a commandment keeps his life;
</para>
  <para style="q1">one who despises his ways will die.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 19:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 19:17"/>One who is gracious {to} a lowly one lends {to} Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and his dealing he will repay to him.
<verse eid="PRO 19:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 19:18"/>Discipline your son when there is hope,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and do not lift up your soul to put him to death.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 19:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 19:19"/>One great of heat lifts up a fine;
</para>
  <para style="q1">for if you rescue, then you will continue to do {so} again.
<verse eid="PRO 19:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 19:20"/>Listen to counsel and accept instruction,
</para>
  <para style="q1">so that you will become wise in your afterwards.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 19:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 19:21"/>Many {are} the plans in the heart of a man,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the counsel of Yahweh, it will stand.
<verse eid="PRO 19:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 19:22"/>The desire of a man {is} his covenant faithfulness,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and better {is} one who is poor than a man of lying.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 19:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 19:23"/>The fear of Yahweh {is} to life
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the satisfied {one} will stay overnight;
</para>
  <para style="q1">he will not be visited by evil.
<verse eid="PRO 19:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 19:24"/>A lazy one hides his hand in the dish;
</para>
  <para style="q1">he will not even return it to his mouth.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 19:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 19:25"/>You strike a mocker and a naive one will become prudent,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and rebuke an understanding one—he will understand knowledge.

<verse eid="PRO 19:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 19:26"/>One who does violence {to} a father, who causes a mother to flee,
</para>
  <para style="q1">{is} a son who causes shame and causes embarrassment.
<verse eid="PRO 19:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 19:27"/>My son, cease to hear instruction
</para>
  <para style="q1">to stray from the words of knowledge.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 19:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 19:28"/>A witness of worthlessness mocks justice,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the mouth of the wicked ones swallows iniquity.
<verse eid="PRO 19:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 19:29"/>Judgments are prepared for the mockers,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and blows for the back of stupid ones.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 19:29"/><verse eid="PRO 19:29"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 19"/>
  <chapter number="20" style="c" sid="PRO 20"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 20:1"/>The wine {is} a mocker, beer {is} a brawler,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and everyone who staggers by it is not wise.
<verse eid="PRO 20:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 20:2"/>The terror of a king {is} a growling like the young lion;
</para>
  <para style="q1">one who infuriates him {is} one who wrongs his life.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 20:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 20:3"/>Honor for a man {is} cessation from strife,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but every fool breaks out.
<verse eid="PRO 20:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 20:4"/>A lazy one will not plow from winter,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he begs in the harvest, but there is nothing.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 20:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 20:5"/>Counsel in the heart of a man {is} deep waters,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but a man of understanding will draw it out.
<verse eid="PRO 20:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 20:6"/>Many a man proclaims, {each} man, his covenant faithfulness,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but a man of faithful acts, who can find?

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 20:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 20:7"/>A righteous {one} walks about in his integrity;
</para>
  <para style="q1">happy {are} his sons after him.
<verse eid="PRO 20:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 20:8"/>A king who sits on the throne of judgment
</para>
  <para style="q1">{is} one who winnows all evil with his eyes.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 20:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 20:9"/>Who can say, “I have made my heart pure;
</para>
  <para style="q1">I am clean from my sin”?
<verse eid="PRO 20:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 20:10"/>Stone and stone, ephah and ephah
</para>
  <para style="q1">{are} an abomination to Yahweh, both the two of them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 20:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 20:11"/>Even a young man will make himself known by his deeds,
</para>
  <para style="q1">if pure and if upright {is} his behavior.
<verse eid="PRO 20:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 20:12"/>A hearing ear and a seeing eye,
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh made both the two of them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 20:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 20:13"/>Do not love sleep lest you become impoverished.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Open your eyes; be satisfied {with} bread.
<verse eid="PRO 20:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 20:14"/>“Bad! Bad!” says the buyer,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but when he departs on his way, then he praises himself.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 20:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 20:15"/>There is gold and an abundance of corals,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but lips of knowledge {are} a vessel of preciousness.
<verse eid="PRO 20:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 20:16"/>Take his garment when he has pledged {for} a stranger,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and on behalf of a foreign woman hold it in pledge.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 20:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 20:17"/>Sweet to a man {is} bread of falsehood,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but afterward his mouth will be filled {with} gravel.
<verse eid="PRO 20:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 20:18"/>Plans by counsel are established,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and by guidance make war.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 20:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 20:19"/>One who goes about {as} a gossip reveals a secret,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and with one who opens his lips do not associate yourself.
<verse eid="PRO 20:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 20:20"/>One who curses his father and his mother,
</para>
  <para style="q1">his lamp will be extinguished in the pupil of darkness.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 20:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 20:21"/>An inheritance gained quickly in the beginning,
</para>
  <para style="q1">its end will not be blessed.
<verse eid="PRO 20:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 20:22"/>Do not say, “I will repay evil.”
</para>
  <para style="q1">Wait for Yahweh, and he will save you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 20:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 20:23"/>Stone and stone {are} an abomination to Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and scales of deceit {are} not good.
<verse eid="PRO 20:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 20:24"/>From Yahweh {are} the steps of a strong man,
</para>
  <para style="q1">so how can a man understand his way?

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 20:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 20:25"/>A snare of a man: He says rashly, “{It is} holy,”
</para>
  <para style="q1">and after vows, considers.
<verse eid="PRO 20:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 20:26"/>A wise king {is} one who winnows the wicked,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he brings back a wheel over them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 20:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 20:27"/>The breath of a man {is} the lamp of Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">searching all the rooms of the belly.
<verse eid="PRO 20:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 20:28"/>Covenant faithfulness and trustworthiness guard a king,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and his throne is sustained by covenant faithfulness.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 20:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 20:29"/>The splendor of young men {is} their strength
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the adornment of old ones {is} gray hair.
<verse eid="PRO 20:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 20:30"/>Blows of a wound cleanse away evil
</para>
  <para style="q1">and strikes, the rooms of the belly.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 20:30"/><verse eid="PRO 20:30"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 20"/>
  <chapter number="21" style="c" sid="PRO 21"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 21:1"/>The heart of a king {is} channels of water in the hand of Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q1">he steers it according to all that he desires.
<verse eid="PRO 21:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 21:2"/>Every way of a man {is} right in his eyes,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but Yahweh examines hearts.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 21:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 21:3"/>To do righteousness and justice
</para>
  <para style="q1">is preferred to Yahweh more than a sacrifice.
<verse eid="PRO 21:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 21:4"/>Height of eyes and broadness of heart,
</para>
  <para style="q1">the lamp of wicked ones, {are} sin.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 21:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 21:5"/>The plans of the diligent {one} surely {are} to profit,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but everyone hurrying about surely {is} to lack.
<verse eid="PRO 21:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 21:6"/>The making of treasures by a tongue of falsehood
</para>
  <para style="q1">{is} scattered vapor, seekers of death.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 21:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 21:7"/>The violence of the wicked will drag them away,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for they refuse to do justice.
<verse eid="PRO 21:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 21:8"/>Perverse {is} the way of a guilty man,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the pure {one}, upright {is} his behavior.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 21:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 21:9"/>Better to dwell on the corner of a roof
</para>
  <para style="q1">than {with} a woman of quarrels and a house of companionship.
<verse eid="PRO 21:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 21:10"/>The soul of the wicked {one} craves evil;
</para>
  <para style="q1">his neighbor is not shown grace in his eyes.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 21:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 21:11"/>When fining a mocker, a naive one becomes wise,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and when giving insight to a wise one, he receives knowledge.
<verse eid="PRO 21:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 21:12"/>A righteous {one} evaluates the house of a wicked {one};
</para>
  <para style="q1">overturning the wicked to evil.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 21:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 21:13"/>One who shuts his ears from the outcry of a lowly one,
</para>
  <para style="q1">he also will cry out but will not be answered.
<verse eid="PRO 21:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 21:14"/>A gift in secrecy subdues nose,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and a bribe in the bosom, strong heat.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 21:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 21:15"/>A joy for the righteous {is} doing justice,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but a terror for doers of iniquity.
<verse eid="PRO 21:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 21:16"/>A man wandering from the way of understanding
</para>
  <para style="q1">will rest in the assembly of the spirits of the dead.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 21:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 21:17"/>A man of lack loves joy;
</para>
  <para style="q1">a lover of wine and oil will not become rich.
<verse eid="PRO 21:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 21:18"/>A ransom for the righteous {one} {is} a wicked {one},
</para>
  <para style="q1">and instead of the upright, one who acts treacherously.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 21:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 21:19"/>Better to dwell in a land of wilderness
</para>
  <para style="q1">than {with} a woman of quarrels and vexation.
<verse eid="PRO 21:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 21:20"/>Desirable treasure and oil {are} in the home of a wise {one},
</para>
  <para style="q1">but a stupid man swallows it up.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 21:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 21:21"/>A pursuer of righteousness and covenant faithfulness
</para>
  <para style="q1">will find life, righteousness, and honor.
<verse eid="PRO 21:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 21:22"/>A wise {one} ascends a city of mighty ones,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he brings down the strength of its confidence.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 21:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 21:23"/>One who keeps his mouth and his tongue
</para>
  <para style="q1">keeps his life from distress.
<verse eid="PRO 21:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 21:24"/>A presumptuous, haughty one, “Mocker” {is} his name,
</para>
  <para style="q1">acting with the rage of presumption.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 21:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 21:25"/>The desire of the lazy one causes him to die,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for his hands refuse to act.
<verse eid="PRO 21:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 21:26"/>All the day he desires desire for himself,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but a righteous {one} gives and does not withhold.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 21:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 21:27"/>The sacrifice of the wicked {is} an abomination;
</para>
  <para style="q1">how much more when he brings it with a wicked plan!
<verse eid="PRO 21:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 21:28"/>A witness of lies will perish,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but a listening man will speak to perpetuity.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 21:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 21:29"/>A wicked man strengthens his face,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but an upright one, he considers his ways.<note style="f" caller="+"> <char style="ft" closed="false">Instead of </char><char style="fqa" closed="true">he considers his ways</char> some read the Hebrew as <char style="fqa" closed="true">he establishes his way.</char></note>

<verse eid="PRO 21:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 21:30"/>There is no wisdom and there is no understanding
</para>
  <para style="q1">and there is no counsel in front of Yahweh.
<verse eid="PRO 21:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PRO 21:31"/>A horse is made ready for the day of battle,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the salvation {is} of Yahweh.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 21:31"/><verse eid="PRO 21:31"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 21"/>
  <chapter number="22" style="c" sid="PRO 22"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 22:1"/>A name is to be chosen more than abundant riches;
</para>
  <para style="q1">favor {is} better than silver and than gold.
<verse eid="PRO 22:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 22:2"/>A rich one and a poor one meet together;
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh {is} maker of all of them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 22:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 22:3"/>A prudent {one} sees evil and hides himself,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the naive pass on and they are fined.
<verse eid="PRO 22:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 22:4"/>The result of humility, the fear of Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">{is} riches and honor and life.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 22:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 22:5"/>Thorns, traps {are} in the way of the crooked;
</para>
  <para style="q1">one guarding his life will stay far away from them.
<verse eid="PRO 22:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 22:6"/>Train up the boy upon the mouth of his way;
</para>
  <para style="q1">even when he is old, he will not turn away from it.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 22:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 22:7"/>A rich one rules over those who are poor,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and a borrower {is} a slave to a man who lends.
<verse eid="PRO 22:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 22:8"/>A sower of iniquity will reap disaster,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the rod of his rage will come to an end.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 22:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 22:9"/>The one good of eye, he will be blessed,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for he gives from his bread to the lowly one.
<verse eid="PRO 22:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 22:10"/>Drive out a mocker and strife will go out,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and judgment and dishonor will cease.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 22:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 22:11"/>One who loves a pure heart,
</para>
  <para style="q1">his lips {are} gracious, the king {is} his friend.
<verse eid="PRO 22:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 22:12"/>The eyes of Yahweh guard knowledge,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but he overturns the words of a treacherous one.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 22:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 22:13"/>A lazy one says, “A lion {is} outside!
</para>
  <para style="q1">I will be killed in the midst of the open areas!”
<verse eid="PRO 22:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 22:14"/>The mouth of a strange woman {is} a deep pit;
</para>
  <para style="q1">one who is cursed of Yahweh will fall there.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 22:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 22:15"/>Folly is bound up in the heart of a boy;
</para>
  <para style="q1">the rod of discipline will cause it to be far away from him.
<verse eid="PRO 22:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 22:16"/>One oppressing a lowly {one} to increase for him,
</para>
  <para style="q1">one giving to the rich, surely {will be} to lack.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 22:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 22:17"/>Incline your ear and hear the words of the wise ones,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and you must set your heart to my knowledge!
<verse eid="PRO 22:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 22:18"/>For {it will be} pleasant if you keep them in your inner parts,
</para>
  <para style="q1">they are ready together on your lips.
<verse eid="PRO 22:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 22:19"/>{For} your trust to be in Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">I have caused you to know today, even you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 22:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 22:20"/>Have I not written for you 30 things<note style="f" caller="+"> <char style="ft" closed="false">Instead of </char><char style="fqa" closed="true">30 things</char>, some manuscripts have <char style="fqa" closed="true">three times.</char> The Hebrew word could also be read as <char style="fqa" closed="true">officers.</char></note>
</para>
  <para style="q1">with counsels and knowledge,
<verse eid="PRO 22:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 22:21"/>to cause you to know the truth of the words of trustworthiness,
</para>
  <para style="q1">to return trustworthy words to one who sent you?

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 22:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 22:22"/>Do not rob a lowly {one} because he {is} a lowly {one},
</para>
  <para style="q1">and do not crush an afflicted {one} at the gate.
<verse eid="PRO 22:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 22:23"/>For Yahweh will plead their dispute,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he will plunder of life those who plunder them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 22:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 22:24"/>Do not befriend an owner of nose,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and do not go {with} a man of heat,
<verse eid="PRO 22:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 22:25"/>lest you learn his paths
</para>
  <para style="q1">and you take a snare for your life.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 22:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 22:26"/>Do not be among those who clasp a palm,
</para>
  <para style="q1">among those who pledge for loans.
<verse eid="PRO 22:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 22:27"/>If there is nothing to you to make payment,
</para>
  <para style="q1">why should he take away your bed from under you?

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 22:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 22:28"/>Do not move the ancient boundary
</para>
  <para style="q1">that your fathers made.
<verse eid="PRO 22:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 22:29"/>You see a skilled man in his work.
</para>
  <para style="q1">He will station himself before the face of kings;
</para>
  <para style="q1">he will not station himself before the face of obscure ones.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 22:29"/><verse eid="PRO 22:29"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 22"/>
  <chapter number="23" style="c" sid="PRO 23"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 23:1"/>When you sit to eat {with} a ruler,
</para>
  <para style="q1">consider carefully what {is} before your face,
<verse eid="PRO 23:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 23:2"/>and you should put a knife at your throat
</para>
  <para style="q1">if you {are} an owner of appetite.
<verse eid="PRO 23:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 23:3"/>Do not desire his delicious morsels,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for it {is} bread of lies.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 23:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 23:4"/>Do not weary yourself to gain riches;
</para>
  <para style="q1">from your understanding, cease.
<verse eid="PRO 23:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 23:5"/>Will you cause your eyes to fly to it, but it is not there?
</para>
  <para style="q1">For making, it will make wings for itself;
</para>
  <para style="q1">like an eagle, it will fly {into} the sky.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 23:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 23:6"/>Do not eat the bread of {one} evil of eye,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and do not desire his delicious morsels.
<verse eid="PRO 23:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 23:7"/>For like one who calculates in his soul, so he {is}.
</para>
  <para style="q1">“Eat and drink!” he will say to you,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but his heart {is} not with you.
<verse eid="PRO 23:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 23:8"/>You will vomit up your morsel you ate,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and you will ruin your pleasant words.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 23:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 23:9"/>Do not speak in the ears of a stupid {one},
</para>
  <para style="q1">for he will show contempt for the insight of your words.
<verse eid="PRO 23:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 23:10"/>Do not move an ancient boundary,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and do not enter into the fields of fatherless ones,
<verse eid="PRO 23:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 23:11"/>for their redeemer {is} strong;
</para>
  <para style="q1">he himself will plead their dispute against you.

<verse eid="PRO 23:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 23:12"/>Bring your heart to correction
</para>
  <para style="q1">and your ear to words of knowledge.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 23:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 23:13"/>Do not withhold discipline from a boy;
</para>
  <para style="q1">when you strike him with the rod, he will not die.
<verse eid="PRO 23:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 23:14"/>You, with the rod you will strike him,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and you will rescue his life from Sheol.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 23:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 23:15"/>My son, if your heart {is} wise,
</para>
  <para style="q1">my heart, even myself, will be glad,
<verse eid="PRO 23:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 23:16"/>and my inner parts will exult,
</para>
  <para style="q1">when your lips speak upright things.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 23:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 23:17"/>Do not let your heart be envious of sinners,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but rather in the fear of Yahweh all the day.
<verse eid="PRO 23:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 23:18"/>Surely there is a future
</para>
  <para style="q1">and your hope will not be cut off.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 23:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 23:19"/>Listen, you my son, and be wise,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and lead your heart in the way.
<verse eid="PRO 23:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 23:20"/>Do not be among drinkers of much wine,
</para>
  <para style="q1">among gluttonous eaters of flesh for themselves.
<verse eid="PRO 23:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 23:21"/>For one who drinks much and one who eats gluttonously will become poor,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and slumber will clothe {with} rags.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 23:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 23:22"/>Listen to your father, this {one} begot you,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and do not despise your mother when she {is} old.
<verse eid="PRO 23:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 23:23"/>Acquire truth and do not sell,
</para>
  <para style="q1">wisdom and instruction and understanding.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 23:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 23:24"/>The father of a righteous one, rejoicing, will rejoice,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and one who begets a wise one, he will be glad in him.
<verse eid="PRO 23:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 23:25"/>May your father and your mother be glad,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and may she who bore you rejoice.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 23:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 23:26"/>My son, give your heart to me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and may your eyes watch<note style="f" caller="+"> <char style="ft" closed="false">Instead of </char><char style="fqa" closed="true">watch</char>, some manuscripts have <char style="fqa" closed="true">desire.</char></note>
my ways.
<verse eid="PRO 23:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 23:27"/>For a prostitute {is} a deep pit,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and a foreign woman {is} a narrow well.
<verse eid="PRO 23:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 23:28"/>Surely she herself lies in wait like a robber,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and she adds to the treacherous ones among man.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 23:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 23:29"/>For whom {is} woe? For whom {is} sorrow? For whom {are} quarrels?
</para>
  <para style="q1">For whom {is} a lament? For whom {are} wounds without reason?
</para>
  <para style="q1">For whom {is} dullness of eyes?
<verse eid="PRO 23:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 23:30"/>For those who linger over wine,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for those coming to search out mixed wine.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 23:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PRO 23:31"/>Do not look {at} wine when it is red;
</para>
  <para style="q1">when its eye gives in the cup,
</para>
  <para style="q1">it goes with evenness.
<verse eid="PRO 23:31"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PRO 23:32"/>Its end bites like a snake,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and it stings like a viper.
<verse eid="PRO 23:32"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PRO 23:33"/>Your eyes will see strange things,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and your heart will speak perverse things.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 23:33"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PRO 23:34"/>And you will be like one who lies down in the heart of the sea
</para>
  <para style="q1">and like one who lies down at the head of a mast.
<verse eid="PRO 23:34"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PRO 23:35"/>“They struck me. I was not hurt.
</para>
  <para style="q1">They beat me. I did not know.
</para>
  <para style="q1">When will I awake? I will add, I will seek it again.”

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 23:35"/><verse eid="PRO 23:35"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 23"/>
  <chapter number="24" style="c" sid="PRO 24"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 24:1"/>Do not be envious of men of evil,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and do not desire to be with them.
<verse eid="PRO 24:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 24:2"/>For their heart plots violence,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and their lips speak trouble.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 24:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 24:3"/>By wisdom a house is built,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and by understanding it is established.
<verse eid="PRO 24:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 24:4"/>And by knowledge the rooms are filled
</para>
  <para style="q1">{with} all precious and pleasant wealth.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 24:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 24:5"/>A man of wisdom {is} with strength
</para>
  <para style="q1">and a man of knowledge strengthens power.
<verse eid="PRO 24:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 24:6"/>For by guidance you make war for yourself
</para>
  <para style="q1">and salvation {is} in an abundance of counsel.

<verse eid="PRO 24:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 24:7"/>Wise things {are too} high for a fool;
</para>
  <para style="q1">at the gate he will not open his mouth.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 24:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 24:8"/>One who plans to do evil,
</para>
  <para style="q1">they will call him an owner of schemes.
<verse eid="PRO 24:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 24:9"/>A scheme of folly {is} sin,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and a mocker {is} an abomination to man.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 24:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 24:10"/>{If} you make yourself slack in the day of distress,
</para>
  <para style="q1">your strength {is} narrow.

<verse eid="PRO 24:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 24:11"/>Rescue those being taken for the death,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and those staggering to the slaughter if you hold back!
<verse eid="PRO 24:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 24:12"/>If you say, “Behold, we did not know this,”
</para>
  <para style="q1">does not he, the examiner of hearts, understand,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he, the guard of your life, know,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he, give back to a man according to his work?

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 24:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 24:13"/>My son, eat honey because {it is} good
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the fresh honey {is} sweet on your palate.
<verse eid="PRO 24:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 24:14"/>Know wisdom {is} thus for your soul;
</para>
  <para style="q1">if you find {it}, then there will be a future
</para>
  <para style="q1">and your hope will not be cut off.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 24:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 24:15"/>Do not lie in wait {like} a wicked {one} against the abode of the righteous;
</para>
  <para style="q1">do not assault his resting place.
<verse eid="PRO 24:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 24:16"/>For seven {times} a righteous {one} falls and rises up,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the wicked stumble into calamity.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 24:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 24:17"/>When your enemy falls, do not be glad,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and when he stumbles, do not let your heart rejoice,
<verse eid="PRO 24:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 24:18"/>lest Yahweh see, and {it be} evil in his eyes,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he turn away his nose from upon him.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 24:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 24:19"/>Do not make yourself hot because of evildoers;
</para>
  <para style="q1">do not envy wicked ones.
<verse eid="PRO 24:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 24:20"/>For a future is not for an evil {one},
</para>
  <para style="q1">the lamp of the wicked will be extinguished.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 24:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 24:21"/>My son, fear Yahweh and the king;
</para>
  <para style="q1">do not associate with ones who change.
<verse eid="PRO 24:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 24:22"/>For suddenly their calamity will arise,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and who {is} knowing the destruction of the two of them?

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 24:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 24:23"/>These also {are} of the wise ones:
</para>
  <para style="q1">Recognizing faces in judgment {is} not good.

<verse eid="PRO 24:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 24:24"/>One saying to a wicked {one}, “You {are} righteous,”
</para>
  <para style="q1">peoples will curse him, nations will denounce him.
<verse eid="PRO 24:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 24:25"/>But for the rebukers it will be pleasant,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and over them will come a blessing of goodness.

<verse eid="PRO 24:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 24:26"/>He kisses lips
</para>
  <para style="q1">who returns straightforward words.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 24:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 24:27"/>Prepare your work in the outdoors,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and make it ready for yourself in the field,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and after, you will build your house.

<verse eid="PRO 24:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 24:28"/>Do not be a witness without cause against your neighbor.
</para>
  <para style="q1">And would you deceive with your lips?
<verse eid="PRO 24:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 24:29"/>Do not say, “Just as he did to me, so I will do to him;
</para>
  <para style="q1">I will return to the man according to his deed.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 24:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 24:30"/>I passed over the field of a lazy man
</para>
  <para style="q1">and over the vineyard of a man lacking of heart.
<verse eid="PRO 24:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PRO 24:31"/>And behold, all of it went up {with} thorns,
</para>
  <para style="q1">its face was covered {with} weeds,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the wall of its stones was torn down.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 24:31"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PRO 24:32"/>And I myself looked, I set my heart,
</para>
  <para style="q1">I saw, I received instruction:
<verse eid="PRO 24:32"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PRO 24:33"/>A little sleep, a little slumber,
</para>
  <para style="q1">a little folding of the hands to lie down,
<verse eid="PRO 24:33"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PRO 24:34"/>and your poverty will come {like} one who walks around,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and your needs like a man of shield.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 24:34"/><verse eid="PRO 24:34"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 24"/>
  <chapter number="25" style="c" sid="PRO 25"/>
  <para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 25:1"/>These also {are} proverbs of Solomon, which the men of Hezekiah, king of Judah, copied.
<verse eid="PRO 25:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 25:2"/>The glory of God {is} to hide a matter,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the glory of kings {is} to search out a matter.
<verse eid="PRO 25:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 25:3"/>Heavens for height and earth for depth,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the heart of kings is not searchable.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 25:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 25:4"/>Remove dross from silver
</para>
  <para style="q1">and a vessel comes out for the refiner.
<verse eid="PRO 25:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 25:5"/>Remove a wicked one to the face of the king,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and his throne will be established by righteousness.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 25:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 25:6"/>Do not honor yourself to the face of the king,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and in the place of the great ones do not stand.

<verse eid="PRO 25:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 25:7"/>For, better to say to you, “Come up here,”
</para>
  <para style="q1">than to humiliate you to the face of a noble,
</para>
  <para style="q1">whom your eyes have seen.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 25:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 25:8"/>Do not go out hastily to dispute,
</para>
  <para style="q1">or else what will you do in its end
</para>
  <para style="q1">when your neighbor humiliates you?

<verse eid="PRO 25:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 25:9"/>Dispute your dispute {with} your neighbor
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the secret of another do not uncover,
<verse eid="PRO 25:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 25:10"/>lest one who hears shame you,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the rumor {of} you not turn back.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 25:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 25:11"/>Apples of gold in sculptures of silver
</para>
  <para style="q2">{is} a word spoken according to its circumstance.
<verse eid="PRO 25:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 25:12"/>A ring of gold and jewelry of fine gold
</para>
  <para style="q1">{is} a wise rebuke to a listening ear.

<verse eid="PRO 25:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 25:13"/>Like the coolness of snow in the day of harvest
</para>
  <para style="q1">{is} a faithful envoy for his senders,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he brings back the life of his masters.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 25:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 25:14"/>Clouds and wind but without rain
</para>
  <para style="q1">{is} the man who boasts in a gift of falsehood.

<verse eid="PRO 25:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 25:15"/>By length of nostrils a commander may be persuaded,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and a soft tongue can break a bone.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 25:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 25:16"/>{If} you find honey, eat enough {for} you,
</para>
  <para style="q1">lest you become satiated with it and you vomit it up.
<verse eid="PRO 25:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 25:17"/>Make rare your foot from the house of your neighbor,
</para>
  <para style="q1">lest he become satiated with you and hate you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 25:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 25:18"/>A hammer and a sword and a sharp arrow
</para>
  <para style="q1">{is} a man who answers a testimony of falsehood against his neighbor.
<verse eid="PRO 25:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 25:19"/>A broken tooth and a shaky foot
</para>
  <para style="q1">{is} confidence {in} one who acts treacherously in the day of distress.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 25:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 25:20"/>One removing a garment on a cold day,
</para>
  <para style="q1">vinegar on natron,
</para>
  <para style="q1">so {is} a singer with songs to a heart of misery.

<verse eid="PRO 25:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 25:21"/>If one who hates you {is} hungry, cause him to eat bread,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and if thirsty, cause him to drink water;
<verse eid="PRO 25:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 25:22"/>for you are heaping embers on his head,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and Yahweh will repay to you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 25:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 25:23"/>The wind of the north brings forth rain,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and indignant faces, a tongue of secrecy.
<verse eid="PRO 25:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 25:24"/>Better to dwell on the corner of a roof
</para>
  <para style="q1">than {with} a wife of quarrels and a house of companionship.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 25:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 25:25"/>Cool water over a weary soul,
</para>
  <para style="q1">so {is} good news from a distant land.
<verse eid="PRO 25:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 25:26"/>A spring muddied by trampling and a fountain spoiled
</para>
  <para style="q1">{is} a righteous {one} swaying to the face of a wicked {one}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 25:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 25:27"/>To eat much honey {is} not good,
</para>
  <para style="q1">also the searching out {of} their honor, honor.
<verse eid="PRO 25:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 25:28"/>A breached city without a wall
</para>
  <para style="q1">{is} a man who has no restraint for his spirit.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 25:28"/><verse eid="PRO 25:28"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 25"/>
  <chapter number="26" style="c" sid="PRO 26"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 26:1"/>Like the snow in the summer and like the rain in the harvest,
</para>
  <para style="q1">so honor {is} not suitable for a stupid one.
<verse eid="PRO 26:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 26:2"/>Like the bird for fluttering, like the swallow for flying,
</para>
  <para style="q1">so a curse without cause does not come.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 26:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 26:3"/>A whip for the horse, a bridle for the donkey,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and a rod for the back of stupid ones.
<verse eid="PRO 26:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 26:4"/>Do not answer a stupid one according to his folly,
</para>
  <para style="q1">lest you yourself also become like him.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 26:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 26:5"/>Answer a stupid one according to his folly,
</para>
  <para style="q1">lest he become wise in his eyes.
<verse eid="PRO 26:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 26:6"/>One cutting off feet, one drinking violence,
</para>
  <para style="q1">{is} one sending words by the hand of a stupid {one}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 26:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 26:7"/>Legs dangle from a lame one,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and a proverb in the mouth of stupid ones.
<verse eid="PRO 26:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 26:8"/>Like tying a stone in a sling,
</para>
  <para style="q1">so {is} one who gives honor to a stupid one.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 26:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 26:9"/>A thorn goes up into the hand of a drunkard,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and a proverb in the mouth of stupid ones.
<verse eid="PRO 26:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 26:10"/>An archer piercing everyone,
</para>
  <para style="q1">so {is} one hiring a stupid {one} and hiring passersby.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 26:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 26:11"/>Like a dog returning to its vomit
</para>
  <para style="q1">{is} a stupid {one} who repeats his folly.
<verse eid="PRO 26:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 26:12"/>You see a man wise in his eyes.
</para>
  <para style="q1">{There is more} hope for a stupid {one} than for him.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 26:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 26:13"/>A lazy {one} says, “A young lion {is} on the road!
</para>
  <para style="q1">A lion {is} between the open areas!”
<verse eid="PRO 26:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 26:14"/>The door turns on its hinge,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and a lazy {one} on his bed.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 26:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 26:15"/>A lazy {one} hides his hand in the dish;
</para>
  <para style="q1">he is {too} weary to return it to his mouth.
<verse eid="PRO 26:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 26:16"/>A lazy {one} {is} wiser in his eyes
</para>
  <para style="q1">than seven returning discernment.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 26:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 26:17"/>One grabbing the ears of a dog passing by
</para>
  <para style="q1">{is} one infuriating himself over a dispute not for him.

<verse eid="PRO 26:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 26:18"/>Like an insane {one} shooting firebrands, arrows, and death,
<verse eid="PRO 26:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 26:19"/>so {is} a man who deceives his neighbor
</para>
  <para style="q1">and says, “Was I not joking?”

<verse eid="PRO 26:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 26:20"/>With the end of wood pieces a fire goes out,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and when there is no murmurer, a quarrel becomes silent.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 26:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 26:21"/>Charcoal to burning coals and wood to fire,
</para>
  <para style="q1">so a man of quarrels {is} to kindling of a dispute.

<verse eid="PRO 26:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 26:22"/>The words of a murmurer {are} like things swallowed greedily,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and they themselves go down into the rooms of the belly.
<verse eid="PRO 26:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 26:23"/>Silver of dross overlaid on a clay vessel
</para>
  <para style="q1">{are} burning lips and a heart of evil.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 26:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 26:24"/>With his lips one who hates disguises himself,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but within him he sets deceit.
<verse eid="PRO 26:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 26:25"/>When he makes his voice gracious, do not trust in him,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for seven abominations {are} in his heart.
<verse eid="PRO 26:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 26:26"/>Hatred is covered by guile;
</para>
  <para style="q1">his evil will be uncovered in the assembly.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 26:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 26:27"/>One who digs a pit will fall into it,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and one who rolls a stone, it will come back to him.
<verse eid="PRO 26:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 26:28"/>A tongue of falsehood hates its oppressed ones,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and a smooth mouth makes calamity.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 26:28"/><verse eid="PRO 26:28"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 26"/>
  <chapter number="27" style="c" sid="PRO 27"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 27:1"/>Do not boast about the next day,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for you do not know what a day will bring forth.
<verse eid="PRO 27:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 27:2"/>Let a stranger praise you and not your mouth,
</para>
  <para style="q1">a foreigner and not your lips.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 27:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 27:3"/>The heaviness of a stone and the weightiness of the sand,
</para>
  <para style="q1">yet the vexation of a fool {is} heavier than the two of them.
<verse eid="PRO 27:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 27:4"/>Cruelty of heat and a flood of nose,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but who can stand to the face of jealousy?

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 27:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 27:5"/>Better {is} open rebuke
</para>
  <para style="q1">than hidden love.
<verse eid="PRO 27:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 27:6"/>Faithful {are} the wounds of one loving,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but deceptive {are} the kisses of one hating.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 27:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 27:7"/>A satiated appetite tramples fresh honey,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but {for} the appetite of a hungry one everything bitter {is} sweet.
<verse eid="PRO 27:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 27:8"/>Like a bird wandering from her nest,
</para>
  <para style="q1">so {is} a man who wanders from his place.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 27:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 27:9"/>Oil and incense gladden the heart,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the sweetness of his friend {is} from the counsel of the soul.
<verse eid="PRO 27:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 27:10"/>Do not forsake your friend and the friend of your father,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and do not enter the house of your brother in the day of your calamity.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Better {is} a nearby inhabitant than a distant brother.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 27:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 27:11"/>Be wise, my son, and gladden my heart
</para>
  <para style="q1">and I shall return a word to one reproaching me.
<verse eid="PRO 27:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 27:12"/>A prudent one sees evil, he hides himself;
</para>
  <para style="q1">naive ones pass on, they are fined.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 27:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 27:13"/>Take his garment when he has pledged {for} a stranger,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and on behalf of a foreign woman hold it in pledge.
<verse eid="PRO 27:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 27:14"/>One who blesses his neighbor with a great voice in the rising morning,
</para>
  <para style="q1">it will be considered a curse to him!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 27:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 27:15"/>A continual dripping on a day of steady rain
</para>
  <para style="q1">and a woman of quarrels are alike.
<verse eid="PRO 27:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 27:16"/>The one hiding her hides the wind,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and oil meets his right hand.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 27:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 27:17"/>Iron sharpens against iron,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and a man sharpens the face of his neighbor.
<verse eid="PRO 27:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 27:18"/>One guarding a fig tree will eat its fruit,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and one protecting his master will be honored.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 27:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 27:19"/>As the water, the face to the face,
</para>
  <para style="q1">so the heart of the man, to the man.
<verse eid="PRO 27:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 27:20"/>Sheol and Abaddon are not satisfied,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the eyes of the man are not satisfied.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 27:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 27:21"/>The smelting-pot {is} for the silver and the furnace {is} for the gold;
</para>
  <para style="q1">so {is} a man for the mouth of one who praises him.
<verse eid="PRO 27:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 27:22"/>Even if you pound a fool in a mortar with a pestle in the midst of ground grains,
</para>
  <para style="q1">his folly will not turn away from on him.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 27:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 27:23"/>Know well the faces of your flock;
</para>
  <para style="q1">set your heart to the herds.
<verse eid="PRO 27:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 27:24"/>For treasure {is} not to eternity,
</para>
  <para style="q1">nor even a crown for generation and generation.
<verse eid="PRO 27:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 27:25"/>The grass disappears, and fresh grass is seen,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the herbs of the mountains are gathered;

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 27:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 27:26"/>lambs {will be} for your clothing,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and male goats the price of a field.
<verse eid="PRO 27:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 27:27"/>And {there will be} enough milk of female goats for your food, for the food of your house,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and life for your young women.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 27:27"/><verse eid="PRO 27:27"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 27"/>
  <chapter number="28" style="c" sid="PRO 28"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 28:1"/>The wicked flee and there is no pursuer,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the righteous are {as} confident as a young lion.
<verse eid="PRO 28:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 28:2"/>By the transgression of a land many {are} its rulers,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but by a man who understands, who knows, so it will endure.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 28:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 28:3"/>A man who is poor and who oppresses the lowly
</para>
  <para style="q1">{is} a rain {that} washes away, and there is no bread.
<verse eid="PRO 28:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 28:4"/>Those forsaking the law praise the wicked,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but those keeping the law strive against them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 28:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 28:5"/>Men of evil do not understand justice,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but seekers of Yahweh understand everything.
<verse eid="PRO 28:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 28:6"/>Better {is} one who is poor who walks in his integrity
</para>
  <para style="q1">than one crooked of ways, yet he {is} rich.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 28:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 28:7"/>One who guards the law {is} a son who understands,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but one who associates with gluttonous eaters humiliates his father.
<verse eid="PRO 28:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 28:8"/>One increasing his wealth by interest and usury
</para>
  <para style="q1">gathers it for one showing favor {to} the lowly.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 28:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 28:9"/>One turning away his ear from hearing the law,
</para>
  <para style="q1">even his prayer {is} an abomination.
<verse eid="PRO 28:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 28:10"/>One leading the upright astray in the way of evil
</para>
  <para style="q1">into his pit he himself will fall,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the blameless will inherit good.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 28:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 28:11"/>A rich man {is} wise in his eyes,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but a discerning lowly {one} will search him out.
<verse eid="PRO 28:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 28:12"/>When the righteous exult, {there is} great splendor,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but when the wicked arise, a man is searched for.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 28:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 28:13"/>One covering his transgressions will not prosper,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but one confessing and forsaking will be shown mercy.
<verse eid="PRO 28:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 28:14"/>Happy {is} a man fearing continually,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but one hardening his heart will fall into evil.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 28:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 28:15"/>A lion growling and a bear charging
</para>
  <para style="q1">{is} a wicked ruler over a lowly people.
<verse eid="PRO 28:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 28:16"/>A leader lacking of understanding {is} also abundant of oppressions;
</para>
  <para style="q1">one hating unjust gain will lengthen days.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 28:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 28:17"/>A man oppressed by the blood of a life
</para>
  <para style="q1">will flee as far as a pit;
</para>
  <para style="q1">let them not support him.
<verse eid="PRO 28:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 28:18"/>One walking blameless will be saved,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but one crooked of ways will fall into one.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 28:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 28:19"/>One working his ground will be satisfied {with} bread,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but one pursuing empty things will be satisfied {with} poverty.
<verse eid="PRO 28:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 28:20"/>A man of faithfulness {has} an abundance of blessings,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but one hurrying to become rich will not remain blameless.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 28:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 28:21"/>Recognizing faces {is} not good,
</para>
  <para style="q1">yet for a bit of bread a man will transgress.
<verse eid="PRO 28:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 28:22"/>One hurrying to the wealth {is} a man of an evil eye,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but he does not know that lack will come to him.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 28:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 28:23"/>One rebuking a man, afterward will find favor
</para>
  <para style="q1">more than one making the tongue smooth.
<verse eid="PRO 28:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 28:24"/>One robbing his father and his mother and says, “There is no transgression,”
</para>
  <para style="q1">he {is} the companion of a man of destruction.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 28:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 28:25"/>One wide of appetite stirs up strife,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but one who trusts in Yahweh will be fattened.
<verse eid="PRO 28:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 28:26"/>One trusting in his heart, he {is} a stupid one,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but one walking in wisdom, he himself will flee.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 28:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 28:27"/>One giving to the one who is poor—there is no lack,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but one hiding his eyes—an abundance of curses.
<verse eid="PRO 28:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 28:28"/>When wicked ones arise, a man will hide himself,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but when they perish, righteous ones will increase.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 28:28"/><verse eid="PRO 28:28"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 28"/>
  <chapter number="29" style="c" sid="PRO 29"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 29:1"/>A man of rebukes who stiffens the neck
</para>
  <para style="q1">will suddenly be broken and without healing.

<verse eid="PRO 29:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 29:2"/>When the righteous increase, the people rejoice,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but when a wicked {one} rules, a people groans.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 29:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 29:3"/>A man who loves wisdom gladdens his father,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but one who associates with prostitutes destroys wealth.
<verse eid="PRO 29:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 29:4"/>A king by justice causes the land to stand,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but a man of contributions tears it down.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 29:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 29:5"/>A man who makes smooth for his neighbor
</para>
  <para style="q1">spreads out a net for his steps.
<verse eid="PRO 29:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 29:6"/>In the transgression of an evil man—a snare,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but a righteous {one} shouts for joy and is glad.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 29:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 29:7"/>A righteous {one} knows the legal claim of the lowly;
</para>
  <para style="q1">a wicked {one} does not understand knowledge.

<verse eid="PRO 29:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 29:8"/>Men of mockery inflame a city,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the wise turn away nose.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 29:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 29:9"/>A wise man goes to judgment with a foolish man,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but he rages and he laughs, and there is no rest.
<verse eid="PRO 29:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 29:10"/>Men of bloodshed hate a blameless {one},
</para>
  <para style="q1">but upright {ones} seek his life.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 29:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 29:11"/>A stupid {one} brings out all his spirit,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but a wise {one} soothes it backward.
<verse eid="PRO 29:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 29:12"/>A ruler who listens attentively to a word of falsehood,
</para>
  <para style="q1">all his servants {are} wicked ones.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 29:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 29:13"/>A poor one and a man of oppression meet together;
</para>
  <para style="q1">the one enlightening the eyes of the two of them {is} Yahweh.
<verse eid="PRO 29:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 29:14"/>A king who judges the lowly with truth,
</para>
  <para style="q1">his throne will be established to perpetuity.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 29:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 29:15"/>A rod and rebuke give wisdom,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but a boy let loose causes his mother shame.
<verse eid="PRO 29:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 29:16"/>When the wicked increase, transgression increases,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the righteous will see their downfall.
<verse eid="PRO 29:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 29:17"/>Discipline your son, and he will cause you to rest,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he will give delights to your soul.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 29:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 29:18"/>When there is no vision, the people are let loose,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but one keeping the law, happy {is} he.

<verse eid="PRO 29:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 29:19"/>A servant will not be instructed by words,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for he understands, but there is no answer.
<verse eid="PRO 29:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 29:20"/>You see a man hurrying in his words.
</para>
  <para style="q1">{There is more} hope for a stupid one than him.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 29:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 29:21"/>Pampering his servant from youth,
</para>
  <para style="q1">then his end will be insolence.
<verse eid="PRO 29:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 29:22"/>A man of nose stirs up strife,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and an owner of heat, much transgression.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 29:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 29:23"/>The pride of a man will make him low,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but {one} lowly of spirit will grasp honor.
<verse eid="PRO 29:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 29:24"/>One who shares with a thief hates his life;
</para>
  <para style="q1">he hears the oath but does not tell.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 29:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 29:25"/>The anxiety of a man sets a snare,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the one trusting in Yahweh will be set on high.
<verse eid="PRO 29:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 29:26"/>Many {are} those who seek the face of a ruler,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but from Yahweh {is} justice of a man.

<verse eid="PRO 29:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 29:27"/>An abomination to the righteous {is} a man of injustice,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but an abomination to the wicked {is} {one} upright of way.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 29:27"/><verse eid="PRO 29:27"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 29"/>
  <chapter number="30" style="c" sid="PRO 30"/>
  <para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 30:1"/>The words of Agur son of Jakeh, the burden:
</para>
  <para style="q1">The declaration of the strong man to Ithiel, to Ithiel and Ucal:
<verse eid="PRO 30:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 30:2"/>“Surely, I {am} more stupid than a man,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the understanding of man {is} not mine.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 30:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 30:3"/>And I have not learned wisdom,
</para>
  <para style="q1">nor the knowledge of holy ones do I know.
<verse eid="PRO 30:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 30:4"/>Who has ascended {to} heaven and descended?
</para>
  <para style="q1">Who has gathered the wind in the hollow of his hands?
</para>
  <para style="q1">Who has wrapped waters in the cloak?
</para>
  <para style="q1">Who has raised up all the ends of the earth?
</para>
  <para style="q1">What {is} his name? And what {is} the name of his son? Surely you know!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 30:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 30:5"/>Every saying of God is refined;
</para>
  <para style="q1">he {is} a shield for those who take refuge in him.
<verse eid="PRO 30:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 30:6"/>Do not add upon his words,
</para>
  <para style="q1">lest he rebuke you and you be shown a liar.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 30:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 30:7"/>Two things I ask from with you,
</para>
  <para style="q1">do not withhold from me before I die:
<verse eid="PRO 30:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 30:8"/>Emptiness and the word of a lie put far away from me.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Do not give to me poverty or riches;
</para>
  <para style="q1">cause me to receive the bread of my portion.
<verse eid="PRO 30:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 30:9"/>Lest I be satiated, and I deny and say, ‘Who {is} Yahweh?’
</para>
  <para style="q1">And lest I become dispossessed and steal,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and I seize the name of my God.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 30:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 30:10"/>Do not slander a slave to his master,
</para>
  <para style="q1">lest he curse you, and you be found guilty.

<verse eid="PRO 30:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 30:11"/>{There is} a generation, it curses its father
</para>
  <para style="q1">and does not bless its mother.
<verse eid="PRO 30:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 30:12"/>{There is} a generation clean in its eyes,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but it is not washed from its excrement.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 30:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 30:13"/>{There is} a generation, how its eyes are raised up,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and its eyelids are lifted up!
<verse eid="PRO 30:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 30:14"/>{There is} a generation, its teeth {are} swords
</para>
  <para style="q1">and its fangs {are} knives
</para>
  <para style="q1">for devouring the afflicted from the earth and the needy from man.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 30:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 30:15"/>Two daughters {are} to the leech, ‘Give! Give!’
</para>
  <para style="q1">{There are} three, they are not satisfied;
</para>
  <para style="q1">four, they do not say, ‘Enough:’
<verse eid="PRO 30:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 30:16"/>Sheol, and the closure of the womb,
</para>
  <para style="q1">a land not satisfied with water,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and a fire—it does not say, ‘Enough!’
<verse eid="PRO 30:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 30:17"/>An eye mocks a father
</para>
  <para style="q1">and shows contempt for the obedience {to} a mother;
</para>
  <para style="q1">the ravens of the valley will peck it out,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the sons of the vulture will eat it.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 30:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 30:18"/>Three things, they {are} too wonderful for me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and four, I do not understand them:
<verse eid="PRO 30:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 30:19"/>the way of the eagle in the sky,
</para>
  <para style="q1">the way of a snake on a rock,
</para>
  <para style="q1">the way of a ship in the heart of the sea,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the way of a young man with a young woman.

<verse eid="PRO 30:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 30:20"/>Thus {is} the way of a woman who commits adultery:
</para>
  <para style="q1">She eats and wipes her mouth
</para>
  <para style="q1">and says, ‘I have not done iniquity.’

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 30:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 30:21"/>Under three things the earth quakes,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and under four it is not able to hold up:
<verse eid="PRO 30:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 30:22"/>under a slave when he becomes king
</para>
  <para style="q1">and a worthless one when he is satisfied with bread,
<verse eid="PRO 30:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 30:23"/>under a hated woman when she is married
</para>
  <para style="q1">and a female servant when she dispossesses her mistress.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 30:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 30:24"/>Four things, they {are} small things of the earth
</para>
  <para style="q1">but they {are} wise things, being made wise:
<verse eid="PRO 30:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 30:25"/>The ants {are} a people not strong,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but they prepare their food in the summer.
<verse eid="PRO 30:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 30:26"/>Rock badgers {are} a people not mighty,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but they set their house in the cliff.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 30:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 30:27"/>There is no king for the locust,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but each of it goes out divided {into groups}.
<verse eid="PRO 30:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 30:28"/>You can catch a lizard with hands,
</para>
  <para style="q1">yet it {is} in the palaces of the king.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 30:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 30:29"/>Three things, they are doing well of step,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and four are doing well of walking:
<verse eid="PRO 30:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 30:30"/>a lion, mighty among the animals,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and it will not turn away from the face of anything,
<verse eid="PRO 30:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PRO 30:31"/>a rooster of loins, or a male goat,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and a king against whom one does not rise up.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 30:31"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PRO 30:32"/>If you have been foolish by lifting up yourself,
</para>
  <para style="q1">or if you have schemed, a hand {be} to mouth!
<verse eid="PRO 30:32"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PRO 30:33"/>For the squeezing of milk brings out butter,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the squeezing of the nose brings out blood,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the squeezing of nostrils brings out strife.”

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 30:33"/><verse eid="PRO 30:33"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 30"/>
  <chapter number="31" style="c" sid="PRO 31"/>
  <para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 31:1"/>The words of Lemuel the king, a burden that his mother had instructed him:
<verse eid="PRO 31:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 31:2"/>What, my son? And what, son of my womb?
</para>
  <para style="q1">And what, son of my vows?
<verse eid="PRO 31:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 31:3"/>Do not give to women your strength
</para>
  <para style="q1">or your ways to cause kings to be wiped out.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 31:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 31:4"/>{It is} not for kings, Lemuel, {it is} not for kings to drink wine
</para>
  <para style="q1">or for dignitaries or intoxicating drink.
<verse eid="PRO 31:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 31:5"/>Lest he drink and forget what has been decreed
</para>
  <para style="q1">and pervert the legal claim of all the sons of the afflicted one.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 31:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 31:6"/>Give intoxicating drink to the perishing one
</para>
  <para style="q1">and wine to those bitter of soul.
<verse eid="PRO 31:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 31:7"/>He will drink and forget his poverty,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and his trouble he will not remember again.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 31:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 31:8"/>Open your mouth for a mute one,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for the legal claim of all the sons of the one passing away.
<verse eid="PRO 31:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 31:9"/>Open your mouth, judge {with} righteousness,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and plead the legal case of the afflicted one and poor one.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 31:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 31:10"/>A woman of worth, who can find?
</para>
  <para style="q1">And her value {is} far more than coral pearls.
<verse eid="PRO 31:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 31:11"/>The heart of her husband trusts in her,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and spoil he will not lack.
<verse eid="PRO 31:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 31:12"/>She does to him good and not evil
</para>
  <para style="q1">all the days of her life.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 31:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 31:13"/>She searches {for} wool and linens
</para>
  <para style="q1">and works with the delight of her palms.
<verse eid="PRO 31:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 31:14"/>She is like the ships of a merchant;
</para>
  <para style="q1">she brings her bread from far away.
<verse eid="PRO 31:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 31:15"/>And she rises while still night
</para>
  <para style="q1">and gives food to her house
</para>
  <para style="q1">and a portion to her young women.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 31:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 31:16"/>She considers a field and gets it;
</para>
  <para style="q1">from the fruit of her palms she plants a vineyard.
<verse eid="PRO 31:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 31:17"/>She girds her loins with strength,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and she strengthens her arms.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 31:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 31:18"/>She perceives that her profit {is} good;
</para>
  <para style="q1">her lamp does not go out in the night.
<verse eid="PRO 31:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 31:19"/>She stretches out her hands at the distaff,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and her palms grasp the spindle.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 31:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 31:20"/>She spreads out her palm to the afflicted one,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and she stretches out her hands to the poor one.
<verse eid="PRO 31:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 31:21"/>She does not fear for her house because of snow,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for all her house is clothed {with} crimson.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 31:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 31:22"/>She makes for herself coverings,
</para>
  <para style="q1">fine linen and purple for her clothing.
<verse eid="PRO 31:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 31:23"/>Her husband is known at the gates,
</para>
  <para style="q1">when he sits with the elders of the land.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 31:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 31:24"/>She makes a linen garment and sells,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and a belt she gives to the Canaanite.
<verse eid="PRO 31:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 31:25"/>Strength and splendor {are} her clothing,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and she laughs at a future day.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 31:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 31:26"/>Her mouth opens with wisdom,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the law of covenant faithfulness {is} on her tongue.
<verse eid="PRO 31:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 31:27"/>She scans the goings on of her house,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the bread of laziness she does not eat.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 31:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 31:28"/>Her sons rise up and call her blessed;
</para>
  <para style="q1">her husband also praises her.
<verse eid="PRO 31:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 31:29"/>“Many daughters have acted {with} worth,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but you yourself have ascended over all of them.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 31:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 31:30"/>The charm {is} falsehood and the beauty {is} vapor;
</para>
  <para style="q1">a woman fearful of Yahweh, she herself will be praised.
<verse eid="PRO 31:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PRO 31:31"/>Give to her from the fruit of her hands
</para>
  <para style="q1">and let her works praise her at the gates.
<verse eid="PRO 31:31"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 31"/>
</usx>
